    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2838?c=isu": {
      "title": "Mechanical Systems Supervisor, Heat Plant - Facilities Services (2245)",
      "description": "Mechanical Systems Supervisor, Heat Plant - Facilities Services (2245) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Mechanical Systems Supervisor, Heat Plant - Facilities Services (2245) United States | req2838 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/13/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Mechanical Systems Supervisor, Heat Plant - Facilities Services (2245) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To plan,\norganize and direct installation, maintenance, and repair of heating,\nventilating, and air conditioning (HVAC) systems; perform related work. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Examples of Duties 1.\nSupervisory. -Interviews and hires staff and evaluates performance. -Supervises personnel assigned to the operation, maintenance, and repair of HVAC and mechanical systems. -Inspects work scheduled and accomplished by staff and contract personnel. -Ensures work meets production and safety standards. -Maintains time, attendance, and related personnel records. -Orients and trains staff in the use and operation of HVAC and related pneumatic and energy systems. -Estimates future needs and cost of repairs and maintenance of HVAC equipment. -Insures adequate staff coverage for shifts and special events. -Plans and implements changes and procedures to conserve energy and utility costs. -Prepares drawings for projects. -Completes paperwork for master logs. -Formulates and monitors maintenance contracts. -Prepares specifications for vendors. 2. HVAC\noperation/maintenance. -Ensures the safe operation, maintenance, and repair of HVAC equipment. -Tests and adjusts component parts, pneumatic control systems, circulation pumps, electronic air cleaners, air filters, regular furnaces, water heaters, piping, and thermostats. -Operates heating and cooling equipment such as boilers, chillers, air conditioners, and cooling towers. -Records balancing and flow data and makes adjustments. -Writes computer programs and operates/changes functions and systems for computerized energy management equipment. -Responds to emergency call backs. Minimum Qualifications Good knowledge\nof: -Reports required and recordkeeping for HVAC control systems. -Computerized HVAC control and fire alarm systems. -Steam distribution systems. -Energy conservation techniques. Some\nknowledge of: -Supervisory practices. Experience: -Operating, maintaining, diagnosing problems and repairing HVAC systems including boilers, air conditioners, chillers, and electric, electronic, and pneumatic heating and cooling controls. -Firing boilers. -Performing electrical repair on HVAC motors, pumps, and related systems. -Preparing specifications for HVAC contracted jobs. -Estimating time and material of HVAC work. -Reading blueprints and specifications for HVAC, electrical, and plumbing installations. Supplemental Information -This work\ninvolves lifting and carrying items weighing approximately 90 pounds, bending,\nstooping, and climbing ladders. Specialty Items -Some\npositions may require the ability to demonstrate successful completion of both\na physical exam, including cardiopulmonary function testing and chest x-ray,\nand a respirator fit test. Additional Information To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before October 28, 2026. Compensation for this opportunity will between $21.25 and $28 per hour,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2838 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: OPERATIONS Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2841?c=isu": {
      "title": "K-12 Program Manager, Albion Institute (2935)",
      "description": "K-12 Program Manager, Albion Institute (2935) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) K-12 Program Manager, Albion Institute (2935) United States | req2841 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/7/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . K-12 Program Manager, Albion Institute (2935) Pocatello or Meridian Campus Hybrid Remote options may be available as approved by the hiring manager Priority Date: October 21, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The K–12 Program Manager oversees the Albion Institute’s K–12 professional learning portfolio and leads its ongoing operations and instructional support functions. The position directly manages educational content specialists and is accountable for portfolio planning, course administration, operational performance, learner engagement, instructional-team coordination, and effective delivery of K–12 offerings. As product manager and the primary program and people leader for K–12 offerings, the Manager establishes product and operational priorities, coaches and evaluates educational content specialists, monitors product and service performance, and coordinates the instructional team. The Manager partners with the Learning Experience Manager, who leads learning-experience strategy, formal instructional quality assurance, development execution, and substantive course redevelopment. The K–12 Program Manager leads ongoing delivery, learner and instructional-team support, operational decision-making, and implementation of approved course and process improvements. This is a promotional opportunity for current employees of Idaho State University only. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Program Operations and Course Administration • Manage the K–12 professional learning portfolio. Lead day-to-day administration, staffing, and operational delivery; establish product and service priorities; assign work; manage dependencies; and ensure accountability for results. • Develop, implement, maintain, and improve operational processes, workflows, documentation, and service standards. Participate in center meetings and processes as invited, representing K–12 product, program, staffing, and learner needs and following through on assigned actions. • Maintain a comprehensive inventory of program needs, operational issues, risks, and enhancement opportunities; resolve routine matters and coordinate appropriate follow-up. Instructional Personnel Supervision and Learner Support • Directly supervise educational content specialists and oversee course graders. Recruit or participate in selection as assigned; establish expectations; assign and review work; provide coaching, training, regular feedback, and performance evaluation; and ensure timely, consistent, high-quality learner support. Coordinate with the Learning Experience Manager when staff assignments involve formal course development, quality reviews, or substantive redesign work. • Coordinate educational content specialists, instructors, teaching assistants, graders, and University partners as an instructional team to address course-delivery needs, resolve issues, and support consistent and effective program operations. • Manage and facilitate online discussion forums that promote meaningful interaction within courses. Ensure educational content specialists and other instructional personnel provide timely check-ins, substantive feedback, and appropriate follow-up to students. • Provide advising to prospective and enrolled learners regarding K–12 professional development offerings, course selection, registration and completion requirements, and program policies. • Connect learners with appropriate University student-support, accessibility, and related services, and coordinate follow-up when additional assistance or intervention is needed. • Coordinate with the Dean of Students and other appropriate University offices to support learners and instructional personnel in addressing student concerns, support needs, and matters requiring specialized assistance or escalation. Develop timely solutions, follow through on agreed actions, and escalate matters requiring specialized assistance or formal review. Refer recurring or systemic concerns that may indicate a learning-design, assessment, accessibility, usability, or product-performance issue to the Learning Experience Manager for evaluation. Course Quality, Performance, and Continuous Improvement • Monitor course delivery, learner feedback, discussion activity, completion rates, service levels, staff and grader performance, student concerns, and other course-health indicators. Use these measures to manage operational performance and provide evidence to the Learning Experience Manager for product evaluation and improvement planning. • Conduct routine post-launch reviews of course content, assessments, learner communications, and course configuration to identify operational, editorial, consistency, accessibility, or learner-support concerns. Correct minor issues within established standards and delegated authority. Document and refer concerns involving learning design, assessment validity, accessibility compliance, multimedia, technical functionality, or substantive redevelopment to the Learning Experience Manager. • Resolve routine delivery and operational issues within delegated authority. Consult the Learning Experience Manager on substantive instructional-design, product-quality, accessibility, development, or redevelopment decisions and coordinate implementation of approved improvement plans. Course Development, Launch, and Program Growth • Represent K–12 operational requirements in the planning and development of new courses, and coordinate operational implementation, launch readiness, and ongoing delivery in partnership with the Learning Experience Manager. Validate staffing and operational readiness, establish post-launch support procedures, receive the completed operational handoff, and manage ongoing delivery following launch. • Maintain accurate product, course, and program information. Assign, review, and approve the work of educational content specialists within established standards and authority. Coordinate substantive instructional, assessment, accessibility, multimedia, or product-design changes with the Learning Experience Manager before implementation. • Develop and maintain the K–12 product roadmap in alignment with Institute priorities. Collaborate with Marketing, the Learning Experience Manager, academic partners, and Institute leadership to evaluate learner and market needs, recommend product enhancements or expansion opportunities, and support portfolio, investment, and lifecycle decisions. Compliance, Reporting, and Decision Support • Monitor program operations for alignment with established institutional policies and quality, compliance, and accessibility standards; address routine issues and escalate matters requiring specialized review or formal determination. • Prepare operational and product-management reports addressing course activity, learner support, student concerns, educational content specialist and grader performance, service levels, product health, operational risks, and improvement needs. Provide relevant evidence to the Learning Experience Manager for product-performance evaluation, improvement planning, and executive reporting. • Recommend K–12 product priorities, investments, enhancements, refreshes, and retirements using operational results, learner outcomes, market information, organizational capacity, financial considerations, and input from the Learning Experience Manager and other partners. Success in this Position Requires • Demonstrated ability to manage an educational product portfolio, lead people and programs, set priorities, monitor employee and course performance, identify operational or instructional issues, make sound decisions, and ensure appropriate follow-through. • Strong organizational, communication, documentation, technology, coaching, and conflict-resolution skills, including the ability to manage multiple priorities, maintain accurate records, prepare reports and updates, and work effectively with students, direct reports, and internal and external partners. Ability to work within shared governance by making timely product, personnel, and operational decisions while consulting the Learning Experience Manager on substantive instructional-design, product-quality, accessibility, development, and redevelopment matters. Ability to occasionally respond to questions or concerns and offer solutions outside regular office hours when urgent course or student needs arise. Minimum Qualifications • To be considered for this position, you must be a current employee at Idaho State University. • Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in education or a related field. • At least three years of progressively responsible professional experience in educational product or program management, educational program administration, continuing education, professional development, online learning, or a related area. • Demonstrated experience coordinating programs, courses, projects, or services involving multiple stakeholders, deadlines, and operational requirements. • Demonstrated experience supervising employees, including assigning work, coaching performance, providing feedback, and supporting professional development. Experience managing instructional or program personnel is preferred. • Experience teaching in a K–12 classroom or providing instructional support in a K–12 educational setting. Preferred Qualifications • Master’s degree from an accredited institution in education or a related field. • Experience administering or supporting professional development, continuing education, or online learning programs for educators. • Experience directly supervising instructional designers, instructors, graders, course facilitators, or other instructional support personnel in an online learning environment. • Familiarity with quality assurance or continuous-improvement practices in online or adult learning environments. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 21, 2026 . Salary will be between $70,000 and $80,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2841 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2840?c=isu": {
      "title": "Financial Technician/Accounting Support, Foundation (2730)",
      "description": "Financial Technician/Accounting Support, Foundation (2730) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Financial Technician/Accounting Support, Foundation (2730) United States | req2840 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/6/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Financial Technician/Accounting Support, Foundation (2730) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To analyze, research,\nforecast, and reconcile complex financial documents; ensure compliance with laws, rules, and policies; perform related work. The Idaho State University Foundation is seeking a proactive, detail-oriented Financial Technician to join our finance team. Working under the direction of the Foundation’s Accounting Manager, the Financial Technician performs a variety of accounting and administrative functions that support the Foundation’s financial operations. The successful candidate will be responsible for maintaining accurate financial records, processing accounts payable and receivable transactions, performing reconciliations, preparing financial reports, and ensuring transactions are properly documented, coded, and approved. This position plays an important role in supporting the Foundation’s financial integrity, compliance, and day-to-day operations. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities -Maintain accurate, complete, and up-to-date financial records. -Process invoices and ensure timely and accurate payments. -Process accounts receivable and ensure accurate coding. -Receive and track payments electronically. -Reconcile bank statements and manage general ledger accounts. -Perform routine account reconciliation and prepare related reports. -Prepare financial reports, summaries, and other financial information as requested. -Review transaction documentation to ensure appropriate coding, required approvals, and adequate supporting documentation. -Support month-end and year-end closing processes. -Review and analyze financial data to identify and resolve discrepancies. -Research financial transactions, account activity, and statements as needed. -Scan, organize, and electronically file financial documents. -Manage and organize accounts payable and accounts receivable communications. -Respond to routine inquiries and direct questions to the appropriate staff member when necessary. -Provide excellent customer service to internal and external customers. -Provide information and assistance to Advancement staff, vendors, donors, and the public. -Work collaboratively with Foundation staff to resolve financial and transaction related questions. -Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications -Some knowledge of financial record keeping. Experience: -Researching and compiling financial\ninformation and preparing summaries and reports. -Using personal computers to enter, retrieve, and edit financial data. Specialty Requirement -These positions at ISU require experience\nusing MS Excel. Additional Information ISU minimum for this classification is $17.25/hour, commensurate with education and experience. To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before October 20, 2026. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2840 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: University Advancement Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2839?c=isu": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Management, College of Business (3313)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Management, College of Business (3313) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate Professor of Management, College of Business (3313) United States | req2839 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/6/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Assistant/Associate Professor of Management, College of Business (3313) Pocatello - Main Hybrid remote may be available as approved by the hiring manager Priority Date: November 1, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description Idaho State University's College of Business seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Management in its Department of Marketing and Management starting August 2027.  The College of Business is accredited by the AACSB. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered Key Responsibilities Teach management classes as needed at the undergraduate and graduate levels in myriad delivery formats (in person, synchronous online, asynchronous online), with primary teaching duties in the area of Supply Chain and operations management. Conduct significant, relevant research in the field leading to publication in respected peer-reviewed scholarly journals. Provide academic and career advising to students and contribute to the advancement of the College and University. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in management (ABD considered if near completion)or closely related field. Candidates at the associate level must have a minimum of six years of full-time college or university teaching at the rank of Assistant Professor (or equivalent) and provide evidence of teaching excellence and evidence of scholarly achievement (as indicated by refereed publications, works under review, and/or works-in-progress). Preferred Qualifications A demonstrated interest in teaching various Supply chain and operations management courses. Other possible secondary areas of interest may include Strategic Management, Entrepreneurship, and/or organization behavior. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 1, 2026 . Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2839 Type: Working 9 months per year Position: Faculty Tenure Track Division: College of Business Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
