    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2837?c=isu": {
      "title": "Clinical Simulation Coordinator/Clinical Instructor, Health Occupations-College of Technology (1855)",
      "description": "Clinical Simulation Coordinator/Clinical Instructor, Health Occupations-College of Technology (1855) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Clinical Simulation Coordinator/Clinical Instructor, Health Occupations-College of Technology (1855) United States | req2837 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/6/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Clinical Simulation Coordinator/Clinical Instructor, Health Occupations-College of Technology (1855) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: November 8, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Simulation coordinator is responsible for supporting and maintaining the functionality of simulation technology in health occupation programs. The coordinator ensures that simulation labs, equipment, and audiovisual systems are operational, maintained, and utilized effectively to support the Health Occupations faculty. This includes the setup, operation, and troubleshooting of simulation technology during nursing simulation sessions and assisting in creating realistic clinical environments for hands-on learning. Additionally, the coordinator manages lab inventory, coordinates scheduling, and assists faculty in the planning and delivery of simulation scenarios. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Technical Operations: •    Set up, operate, and break down simulation scenarios, including high-fidelity manikins, medical equipment, and audiovisual systems. •    Prepare environments to simulate healthcare-related experiences, including moulage application for realism. •    Operate simulation software and systems to ensure that physiological responses occur per faculty specifications. •    Troubleshoot and maintain simulation equipment and software to ensure consistent operation. •    Utilize the audiovisual system (e.g., Simcapture) for clear recordings of simulation scenarios and troubleshoot issues as needed. •    Program manikins and simulation technology according to scenario learning objectives. •    Function as the voice of simulators and coach embedded participants on developed roles. Simulation Support and Coordination: •    Collaborate with faculty to design, implement, and deliver simulation scenarios. •    Assist faculty and students in operating simulation technology during hands-on training. •    Coordinate scheduling of simulation labs and equipment in collaboration with faculty. •    Support the use of standardized patients and assist in selecting appropriate modalities for simulation scenarios. •    Assist with debriefing learners and faculty according to best practices. •    Engage with community partners to provide simulation opportunities. Maintenance and Inventory: •    Perform routine maintenance of simulation equipment, manikins, and audiovisual technology. •    Manage inventory systems, ensuring simulation environments are stocked with necessary medical supplies and equipment. •    Restock labs after simulation scenarios and coordinate the ordering of supplies. •    Ensure the proper care and maintenance of all simulation technology and equipment. Training and Professional Development: •    Train faculty, staff, and students on the use of simulation equipment and software. •    Participate in continual learning, including staying up-to-date with advancements in simulation technology. Data Collection and Reporting •    Document simulation activities, including equipment usage, technical issues, and maintenance logs. •    Assist with data collection for program evaluation and student assessment purposes. •    Collaborate with faculty on curriculum design and simulation scenario planning. Minimum Qualifications •    Bachelor’s degree in healthcare related field. •    Knowledge of audiovisual equipment, and simulation technology. •    Understanding of medical terminology and healthcare practices. •    Strong troubleshooting skills for simulation equipment, technology, and software. •    Ability to work collaboratively with faculty and students. •    Strong oral communication and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications •    Experience with high-fidelity simulation systems (e.g., Laerdal, Gaumard, or CAE) and audiovisual systems (e.g., Simcapture). •    Experience working in an educational or clinical healthcare setting. •    Knowledge of audiovisual recording systems, database management, and inventory management systems. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 8, 2026 . Salary will be between $60,000 and $75,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2837 Type: Working 11 months per year Position: Faculty Non-Tenure Track Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2836?c=isu": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Cancer Pharmacology and Cell Biology (2929)",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Cancer Pharmacology and Cell Biology (2929) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Postdoctoral Researcher, Cancer Pharmacology and Cell Biology (2929) United States | req2836 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Postdoctoral Researcher, Cancer Pharmacology and Cell Biology (2929) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: November 5, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Zeleke Therapeutic Development Laboratory in the Department of Biomedical Sciences at the L. S. Skaggs College of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Idaho State University, invites applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher to join our funded cancer drug discovery program. This is a full-time position with up to two years of support, contingent upon satisfactory performance and continued funding. Our laboratory focuses on the discovery and development of innovative small-molecule therapeutics for cancer. The successful candidate will contribute to projects aimed at developing next-generation anticancer agents and will have opportunities to publish research findings, present at scientific meetings, and mentor graduate and undergraduate trainees. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities -Design and conduct cellular, molecular, and pharmacological studies to evaluate the activity, mechanism of action, target engagement, and resistance mechanisms of novel anticancer compounds. -Perform mammalian cell culture and assays including viability, proliferation, apoptosis, cell-cycle analysis, Western blotting, and related protein-based techniques. -Conduct and support preclinical animal studies to evaluate antitumor efficacy, pharmacology, and tolerability of lead compounds. -Analyze and interpret experimental data and collaborate with medicinal chemistry and computational researchers to guide compound prioritization and optimization. -Prepare manuscripts, abstracts, posters, and scientific presentations, and contribute to mentoring graduate and undergraduate trainees. -Maintain accurate research records and comply with laboratory, biosafety, and animal-research requirements. Minimum Qualifications -Ph.D. in Cancer Biology, Pharmacology, Molecular Biology, or a related discipline. -Experience with mammalian cell culture, molecular biology, flow cytometry, Western blotting, microscopy, drug screening, or related experimental techniques. -Excellent communication skills and a strong publication record or demonstrated research productivity. Preferred Qualifications -Experience in anticancer drug discovery. -Experience with in vivo tumor models and preclinical animal studies. -Strong publication record and demonstrated ability to contribute to independent and collaborative research projects. -Experience mentoring undergraduate or graduate trainees. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, a one-page statement of research interests and career goals, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 5, 2026 . Salary will be $57,444 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2836 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Kasiska Division of Health Sciences Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2833?c=isu": {
      "title": "Director of Graduate Studies, College of Business (3416)",
      "description": "Director of Graduate Studies, College of Business (3416) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Director of Graduate Studies, College of Business (3416) United States | req2833 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Director of Graduate Studies, College of Business (3416) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: November 5, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Director of Graduate Programs provides strategic leadership and oversight for graduate student services within the College of Business. This position is responsible for managing graduate advising, recruitment, admissions coordination, and student success initiatives while supporting program quality, enrollment growth, retention, and timely degree completion. The Director of Graduate Programs collaborates closely with faculty, program directors, and administrative units to enhance graduate program delivery, support accreditation and assessment efforts, and ensure a high-quality, student-centered experience across all graduate programs. Travel is required for this position (Approximately 1-3 days per week during recruiting seasons, including overnight stays.) This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Graduate Program Leadership & Strategy • Provide leadership for College of Business graduate programs and student services, supporting enrollment, retention, student progression, and continuous improvement. • Collaborate with the Dean, Associate Dean, faculty, and department leadership on curriculum, program needs, strategic initiatives, and fall, spring, and summer course scheduling. • Advise on graduate curriculum, catalog requirements, degree pathways, course substitutions, and institutional policies. Participate in committees related to graduate education and serve on the Graduate Faculty Committee. Admissions, Recruitment & Advising • Lead graduate recruitment and admissions, including recruitment activities, application processes, prospective student communication, campus visits, and outreach events. • Oversee graduate advising throughout the student lifecycle, including onboarding, academic planning, study plans, petitions, appeals, overrides, degree audits, graduation checks, and teach-out plans. • Develop communication and onboarding strategies supporting registration, engagement, retention, timely progression, and degree completion. • Collaborate with Admissions and Marketing and Communication on targeted recruitment strategies for domestic, international, online, and other priority groups. Accreditation, Assessment & Operations • Support accreditation and program review through graduate program data collection, reporting, documentation, and analysis of enrollment, retention, progression, and student outcomes. • Supervise graduate assistants, including selection input, onboarding, training, and assignment coordination. • Oversee graduate scholarship administration and operational processes supporting graduate programs. • Serve as liaison with the Graduate School, Admissions, Registrar, Financial Aid, Scholarship Office, and other campus partners. Minimum Qualifications •    Master's degree from a regionally accredited university. •    Two years of experience in academic advising, student services, or a related higher education setting, including professional, mentoring, peer advising, or similar student support experience. •    Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. •    Excellent organizational management and human relation skills. •    Efficient with technology (Word, Excel, Google Docs). Preferred Qualifications •    Solid working knowledge of student development, academic advising, and student services within a higher education setting. •    Four years of experience in academic advising, student services, or a related field within higher education. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 5, 2026 . Salary will be between $67,000 and $72,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2833 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2831?c=isu": {
      "title": "K-12 Program Coordinator, Albion Institute (2930)",
      "description": "K-12 Program Coordinator, Albion Institute (2930) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) K-12 Program Coordinator, Albion Institute (2930) United States | req2831 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/1/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . K-12 Program Coordinator, Albion Institute (2930) Pocatello or Meridian Campus Hybrid Remote options may be available as approved by the hiring manager Priority Date: October 15, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description This\nis a promotional opportunity for current, employees of Idaho State University only. The K-12 Program Coordinator supports the day-to-day administration and delivery of the Albion Institute’s K-12 professional learning program. Working under the direction of the K-12 Program Manager, the position coordinates course administration, supports educational content specialists, instructors, and graders, monitors routine course delivery, and helps ensure offerings are delivered efficiently and consistently with established Institute and University standards. The Coordinator carries out established operational workflows, maintains accurate program information and documentation, provides direct learner and instructional-team support, addresses routine administrative issues, and implements approved course and process updates. The Coordinator supplies timely operational information to the K-12 Program Manager, who serves as product manager, supervises program personnel, establishes priorities, makes product and operational decisions, and coordinates substantive learning-design, quality, development, and redevelopment matters with the Learning Experience Manager. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Program Operations and Course Administration •    Coordinate of K–12 professional development courses under the K–12 Program Manager’s direction. •    Maintain course, learner, personnel, and program records and issue logs; resolve routine matters and escalate significant or recurring issues. Instructional Team and Learner Support •    Coordinate onboarding, schedules, communications, documentation, and support for instructional personnel; flag workload, performance, or service concerns. •    Monitor learner support and facilitate online discussion forums and check-ins as assigned. Advise learners on offerings, course selection, registration, completion, and policies; document follow-up. •    Connect learners with University support and accessibility services. Escalate concerns requiring specialized assistance, formal review, or product evaluation. •    Provide Tier 2 support for escalated customer-service matters. Resolve complex course, registration, access, policy, and learner-support issues within assigned authority; document outcomes and elevate sensitive or unresolved matters. Course Quality, Performance, and Continuous Improvement •    Track course activity, feedback, completion, service levels, grader activity, and student concerns; report exceptions to the K–12 Program Manager. •    Check post course launch content, assessments, communications, links, and course configuration against standards. Correct minor administrative or editorial issues and refer instructional, accessibility, multimedia, technical, or redevelopment concerns. •    Implement approved course and operational updates, monitor results, and coordinate with the Learning Experience Manager or other partners as assigned. Course Development, Launch, and Program Growth •    Complete assigned launch and handoff tasks for new or revised courses, including staffing preparation, setup, documentation, learner communications, and support procedures; maintain records and verify updates. •    Support approved marketing by maintaining accurate program information and coordinating materials with the marketing team. Compliance, Reporting, and Decision Support •    Monitor assigned activities against quality, compliance, and accessibility standards; address routine issues and escalate potential noncompliance. •    Prepare reports and maintain evidence on course delivery, learner and instructional-team support, service levels, issues, and implementation progress to inform the K–12 Program Manager’s decisions. Minimum Qualifications •    To be considered for this position, you must be a current employee in good standing at Idaho State University. •    Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in education or a related field. •    At least three years of professional experience in program coordination, educational program administration, continuing education, professional development, online learning, or a related area. •    Demonstrated experience coordinating programs, courses, projects, or services involving multiple stakeholders, deadlines, and operational requirements. •    Experience supporting instructors, faculty, educational content specialists, graders, facilitators, or other instructional or program personnel. •    Experience teaching in a K-12 classroom or providing instructional support in a K-12 educational setting. Preferred Qualifications •    Project Management Professional Certification •    Experience administering or supporting professional development, continuing education, or online learning programs for educators. •    Experience supporting instructors, graders, facilitators, or other instructional support personnel. •    Familiarity with quality assurance or continuous-improvement practices in online or adult learning environments. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 15, 2026 . Salary will be between $50,000 and $58,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2831 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2829?c=isu": {
      "title": "Employee Relations & Leave Administration Specialist, Human Resources (3180)",
      "description": "Employee Relations & Leave Administration Specialist, Human Resources (3180) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Employee Relations & Leave Administration Specialist, Human Resources (3180) United States | req2829 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/29/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Employee Relations & Leave Administration Specialist, Human Resources (3180) Pocatello - Main Hybrid remote available as approved by the hiring manager Priority Date: October 30, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Employee Relations & Leave Administration Specialist provides operational support for the Employee Relations function, with primary responsibility for the independent administration of FMLA and assigned leave programs. This role manages leave cases from inquiry to closure, ensuring accurate tracking and timely communication with employees, supervisors, and key university partners (Payroll, Benefits, ADA, Workers' Compensation). Additionally, this role supports Employee Relations by handling concern intake, case management, and administrative coordination, escalating high-risk matters to leadership as needed. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities FMLA and Leave Administration – 65% -Case Ownership: Serve as the primary point of contact for FMLA, managing all stages of the leave process, from initial intake and eligibility determination to return-to-work and case closure. -Documentation & Compliance: Manage all notices, medical certifications, and leave tracking. Proactively identify documentation deficiencies, monitor intermittent/reduced-schedule usage, and ensure accurate record-keeping. -Communication & Guidance: Educate employees and supervisors on FMLA policies, roles, and responsibilities. Maintain consistent communication regarding leave status, return-to-work requirements, and employee protections. -Process Coordination: Integrate FMLA with other University programs, including ADA accommodations, workers' compensation, paid leave, and the Shared Leave Donation Program. Ensure accurate payroll processing and facilitate timely return-to-work coordination. -Training & Improvement: Serve as a subject matter expert. Develop job aids, deliver training, and recommend process improvements to ensure consistent policy application. Employee Relations Support – 25% -Concern Intake: Act as an initial point of contact for employee/supervisor workplace concerns. Conduct objective preliminary intake and route to appropriate staff or leadership. Escalate high-risk matters (e.g., discrimination, harassment, safety concerns) immediately. -Administrative Support: Coordinate meetings, trainings, and interviews. Prepare and format letters, memoranda, and investigative materials. Maintain secure, confidential records and track case-related deadlines. General HR Support – 10% -Maintain accurate HR records, assist with departmental reporting, and contribute to HR projects, training programs, and policy implementation. Minimum Qualifications -Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Public Administration, or a related field (in lieu of a Bachelor’s Degree, a minimum of six years combined education, training, and experience may be considered). -At least two (2) years of professional experience in human resources, employee relations, compliance, leave or benefits administration, or a related field, including handling confidential, sensitive, medical, personnel, or employment-related information. -Strong organizational and problem-solving skills; ability to manage multiple deadlines with high accuracy and maintain confidentiality. -Proven ability to interpret/apply policies and exercise sound judgment in escalating sensitive or complex matters. -Excellent communication and customer service skills. Preferred Qualifications -Direct experience administering FMLA, coordinating with ADA/workers' compensation, and utilizing HR information/case-management systems. -Experience in workplace investigations or supporting Employee Relations functions. -Experience in higher education or public-sector HR environments. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 30, 2026 . Salary will be between $50,000 and $55,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2829 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: OPERATIONS Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2827?c=isu": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance, College of Business (3312)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance, College of Business (3312) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance, College of Business (3312) United States | req2827 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/22/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance, College of Business (3312) Pocatello - Main Eligible for a hybrid remote work schedule, as approved by the hiring manager Priority Date: October 16, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Department of Economics & Finance in the College of Business at Idaho State University invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance in the field of corporate finance and/or investments beginning August 2027. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in face-to-face or online modes as needed by the department, conduct field-related research leading to publications in peer-reviewed scholarly journals, and engage in service-related activities. Teaching load requirements are three courses in both Spring and Fall semester. It is anticipated the individual filling this roll will teach Corporate Financial Management at least once per semester and Advanced Corporate Finance at least once per year, with the balance of classes determined by departmental needs. The candidate will be required to maintain AACSB academic qualifications as a Scholarly Academic. Minimum Qualifications The successful candidate will have earned, or be close to completing, a doctorate in Finance (Ph.D. or DBA) by the time of hire, with an emphasis in corporate finance and/or investments. The successful candidate will also desire to live in the intermountain west and teach at a regional-serving institution of first access. Candidates seeking to be hired at the rank of Associate Professor must have a minimum of 6 years of experience at the Assistant Professor rank, evidence of teaching excellence, and evidence of scholarly achievement. Preferred Qualifications A highly qualified candidate will demonstrate the ability to successfully teach students from broad backgrounds and possess a willingness to engage with students both in and out of the classroom. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 16, 2026 . Salary will be between $130,000 and $145,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2827 Type: Working 9 months per year Position: Faculty Tenure Track Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2825?c=isu": {
      "title": "Chair/Director/Clinical Assistant Prof, Idaho Advanced Education General Dentistry Residency (2127)",
      "description": "Chair/Director/Clinical Assistant Prof, Idaho Advanced Education General Dentistry Residency (2127) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Chair/Director/Clinical Assistant Prof, Idaho Advanced Education General Dentistry Residency (2127) United States | req2825 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/22/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Chair/Director/Clinical Assistant Prof, Idaho Advanced Education General Dentistry Residency (2127) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Open until filled Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The department chair and program director is responsible for the Idaho Advanced Education in General Dentistry Residency (IAGD). The program mission statement reads: The Idaho Advanced General Dentistry Program’s mission is to provide an outstanding educational environment where dental residents advance their knowledge and experience over that obtained in the pre-doctoral curriculum and develop a sense of personal responsibility for continued learning and constantly advancing clinical skills while providing caring, competent services to their patients. The department chair and program director is expected to participate in, appoint and oversee all operational aspects of the program. This position is .50 FTE (20 hours per week) to 1.0 FTE (40 hours per week) depending upon the successful candidate. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered Key Responsibilities Responsible for the overall educational, clinical, operational, and accreditation oversight of the Dental Residency Program, ensuring residents achieve the competencies and proficiencies required for successful program completion. Develop, implement, and continuously evaluate the program curriculum, including clinical rotations, scheduling, didactic instruction, distance learning, and external clinical experiences, ensuring appropriate integration of educational and clinical components. Design and implement outcomes assessment processes to evaluate resident achievement, program effectiveness, and opportunities for continuous improvement. Teach didactic courses as needed and participate in at least 20% clinical teaching of dental residents. Provide overall leadership and accountability for the Pocatello Family Dentistry Clinic and ISU Family Dentistry Clinic in Meridian, including operational effectiveness, budgetary oversight, public service, and coordination with clinic leadership. Supervise and provide leadership for residency program employees, residents, and faculty, while maintaining definitive authority and responsibility for program and site activities in collaboration with Site Directors. Develop and maintain strong relationships with the dental community, professional organizations, local and state dental societies, State Boards of Dentistry and Education, civic organizations, and other external partners. Lead recruitment efforts at dental schools and other appropriate venues to attract highly qualified residents and support recruitment and retention of high-quality faculty. Maintain full responsibility for program accreditation through the American Dental Association Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA), including preparation of self-studies, progress reports, and other required accreditation materials, and ensure ongoing compliance with CODA standards. Maintain active faculty responsibilities and ensure continuity and consistency between the Pocatello and Meridian program sites, including travel between sites at least monthly as required to support program operations and CODA standards. Develop external partnerships and pursue sponsorships and other funding opportunities that support the program and its educational and clinical mission. Minimum Qualifications Earned DDS or DMD degree followed by a completion of an AEGD or GPR dental program with a current license and eligible for licensure in the State of Idaho. A minimum of 5 (five) years of experience of Clinical practice in a dental setting. Ability to travel to sister site monthly to assure program consistency in both residency locations. Experience with budget planning and management. Ability to develop relationships and work cooperatively with local dentists and dental schools. Ability to effectively develop curriculum for the residents. Commitment to building necessary partnerships to increase excellence in the residency program. Communication, trust, transparency. Preferred Qualifications Successful experience in strategic planning that fosters collaborative work with faculty to maintain and develop current, evidence based, practices in dentistry and develop strategies to achieve this in the residency program. Possess outstanding creative, forward thinking skills, the ability to make informed decisions, and effectively communicate the rationale for decisions. Experience with accreditation agencies. A commitment to professional, community service based residency program with the expectation of high quality dentistry to be taught to and performed by dental residents. Ability to practice dentistry in a faculty based practice on-site. Certified in IV Sedation Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled . Salary is competitive and commensurate with education, experience, and appointment status (full-time or part-time). Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2825 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Faculty Non-Tenure Track Division: Division of Health Sciences Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2824?c=isu": {
      "title": "International Student Advisor, International Programs Office (2926)",
      "description": "International Student Advisor, International Programs Office (2926) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) International Student Advisor, International Programs Office (2926) United States | req2824 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/21/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . International Student Advisor, International Programs Office (2926) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: October 21, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The successful candidate will serve as an immigration advisor to international students and serves as a Designated School Official (DSO).  Completes immigration paperwork as well as issue, file and monitor immigration documents and applications. Responsible for updating student records in the federal government SEVIS system using ISSM for batch submissions to the SEVIS database; ensures the university’s continuing compliance with SEVIS reporting requirements and other federal reporting requirements. Key Responsibilities •    Serve as an advisor, advising and assisting international students regarding F-1 and J-1 immigration requirements, and prepare appropriate federal documents for work authorization and visa related requests. Advises students on the U.S. immigration, laws, and regulations that impact their enrollment and continued stay in the United States. Process I-20 and DS-2019 applications for new and continuing international students and ensure applications materials meet the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) requirements. Advise students on how to maintain enrollment status as per immigration regulations, and assist students in filing applications with DHS. Verify student enrollment, enters/updates immigration information to student database (ISSM). Maintains I-20 and DS-2019 forms and documentations used by the International Programs Office to assist students with applications and immigration issues. •    Stay informed of current immigration regulations and requirements and maintains professional knowledge of international regulatory policies affecting Idaho State University students and community. Functions as a Designated School Official (DSO) and Alternate Responsible Officer (ARO) for the university’s F and J programs. •    Represents the office at various meetings and serve on inter-office committees or teams in collaborative efforts as required. Advise international student organizations. Plans and delivers various workshops throughout the year. Coordinates cultural and social events and services to assist new students upon their arrival to Pocatello and Idaho State University. Assist with coordination of international student orientation for each semester. •    Tracks students’ admission and the whereabouts of former international students. Tracks and report enrollment numbers and all other international student data each semester. •    Other duties as assigned, maintains confidentiality as appropriate. Minimum Qualifications •    Bachelor’s degree and at least one (1) year working within in a higher education setting. •    Ability to serve as a Designated School Official (DSO). •    Per Federal regulations governing F-1 and J-1 visa program sponsors, candidate must be a US citizen or permanent resident. •    Working knowledge of F-1 and J-1 federal regulations. •    Accuracy and attention to detail. •    Demonstrated experience recognizing political ramification and/or consequences of situations related to self, and/or institution. Analyzing the impact of actions and situations and to use good judgement in responding and or referring or consulting with others. •    Must be able to function independently, be motivated, and show good judgment in leadership and conflict resolution skills. •    Ability to model professional behavior, enlist others in a common vision; provide innovative ideas and facilitate collaboration. Preferred Qualifications •    Master’s degree and at least three (3) years working within an academic setting in the area of international immigration advising. •    One (1) year of experience as a Designated School Official (DSO). •    Experience utilizing Ellucian Banner, Slate and ISSM databases. •    Expertise in the use of the federal SEVIS database. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 21, 2026 . Salary will be $49,750 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2824 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Enrollment Management Admin Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2823?c=isu": {
      "title": "Instruction Assistant, Aircraft Maintenance Technology (1969)",
      "description": "Instruction Assistant, Aircraft Maintenance Technology (1969) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Instruction Assistant, Aircraft Maintenance Technology (1969) United States | req2823 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/18/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Instruction Assistant, Aircraft Maintenance Technology (1969) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To\nprovide instruction and tutoring as an assistant to an academic teacher in a\nstate facility or university; perform related work. The successful candidate will provide support to the Aircraft Maintenance Technology program and to the instructors in non-instructional capacities to include: tool control, inventory tracking, facility and equipment maintenance, safety monitoring, purchasing, and administrative support. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities -Manage tools, parts, and equipment inventory. -Manage facilities and equipment to include physical security, submitting maintenance/work requests, and facilitating equipment repairs. -Purchase parts and supplies as needed, and manage P-Card, including keeping financial records. -Monitor safety in the laboratory, involve the Program Coordinator as needed. -Maintain and organize program and student records as needed. -Interact with the public, other ISU employees, vendors, and the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) in capacities including; answering phones, greeting visitors, coordinating with vendors, scheduling maintenance and deliveries, and assisting with program recruiting efforts. -Support program instructors as needed. Minimum Qualifications Some\nknowledge of: -Behavioral management as related to an educational environment. Experience: -Presenting lesson plans and educational materials to students. -Working in a group education setting, -Entering and retrieving data and maintaining records using an automated record system, -Typing labels, lists, forms and reports, Supplemental Information This position at ISU involves the physical ability to bend, stoop,\nlift and move items weighing up to 50 pounds and work in hot and humid\nenvironments. Additional Information ISU minimum for this classification is $16.75/hour, commensurate with education and experience. To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before October 19, 2026. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2823 Type: Working 11 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
