    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2822?c=isu": {
      "title": "Utility Craftsman Senior, Idaho Falls University Programs (1564, 2508)",
      "description": "Utility Craftsman Senior, Idaho Falls University Programs (1564, 2508) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Utility Craftsman Senior, Idaho Falls University Programs (1564, 2508) United States | req2822 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/18/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Utility Craftsman Senior, Idaho Falls University Programs (1564, 2508) Idaho Falls NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Located along the Snake River, the ISU Idaho Falls campus provides hands-on learning through over 100-degree programs. To support this mission, we operate with a small, unified team utilizing a shared-service model. Our employees collaborate across traditional departmental boundaries to optimize resources, streamline operations, and maintain the operational excellence essential to student success. Job Description The successful candidate will perform and direct advanced journey-level and master-level construction, building trades, mechanical work, and grounds maintenance in multiple areas of responsibility related to constructing facilities and maintaining associated systems and equipment on the Idaho Falls campus of Idaho State University. Work hours are typically between 6 a.m. – 3:30 p.m., Monday through Friday. On call and after-hours work is a regular function of this position due to the nature of the responsibilities. This position is not eligible for remote work. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Construction & Building Trades -Lead and perform structural construction and remodeling, including framing, drywall, siding, painting, and installation of doors/locks. -Perform specialized masonry, steel erection, and finish carpentry. -Execute concrete work, including forming, pouring, finishing, and repair of flatwork and foundations. -Operate heavy construction equipment, including excavators, backhoes, loaders, and dump trucks. Mechanical & Systems Maintenance -Maintain and repair electrical systems, including wiring, lighting, ballasts, and switches. -Perform plumbing repairs on pipes, fixtures, septic systems, and gas lines. -Maintain and repair small engines, hydraulic systems, and diesel-powered equipment. Landscaping & Grounds Management -Execute end-to-end grounds care, including lawn maintenance, horticultural management, and campus forestry. -Install, troubleshoot, and maintain automated irrigation systems; implement water conservation practices. -Manage year-round site safety through consistent snow and ice removal and hazardous tree mitigation. -Design and construct new landscape projects, including site prep and hardscape installation. Event Logistics & Safety -Support campus events by interpreting diagrams to set up and tear down staging, tables, chairs, and program aids. -Ensure all event layouts maintain symmetry, proper spacing, and strict compliance with fire safety and ADA guidelines. -Perform traffic control, site safety inspections, and manage hazardous materials as needed. Project Support and Coordination -Review project plans, blueprints, and specifications to ensure compliance and quality. -Conduct on-site inspections, coordinate with contractors and regulatory agencies, and manage project modifications. -Compute material quantities, oversee costs, and manage contractor/supplier payments. -Maintain detailed project reports and provide input on staff performance. All reasonable duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Considerable\nknowledge of: -Construction and building trades work. -Construction methods. Experience: -Operating, transporting and maintaining equipment\nassociated with construction and building trades and grounds maintenance. -Placing and finishing concrete. -Performing rough and finish carpentry. -Performing maintenance plumbing and electrical work. -Reading/interpreting plans, specifications and blueprints. -Using and maintaining building trades hand and power tools. -Providing construction and trades direction and training to\nothers. -Evaluating the construction and trades performance of\nothers. -Identifying, procuring and organizing materials and\nequipment necessary for construction projects. Specialty Requirements - These\npositions at ISU require the following: -Valid\ndriver's license. -Respond\nto emergency call-backs. -Successful\ncompletion of both a physical exam, including cardiopulmonary function testing\nand chest x-ray, as well as a respirator fit test. Supplemental Information The\nincumbent is considered an advanced journey-level and master-level worker in\nall aspects of inside and outside heavy construction and building trades type\nwork. This is primarily new construction, although maintenance of existing\nfacilities may be included. Incumbents should have a proficient background in\nall aspects of construction and trades work. This\nposition requires you to work in all weather conditions. This\nposition also involves physical activities associated with construction work\nsuch as lifting and carrying items weighing approximately 100 pounds, bending\nand stooping, and working at heights of up to 50 feet. Some positions,\ndepending on department needs, may require registration and training as a\nplumbing or electrical apprentice. Additional Information ISU minimum for this classification is $21.25/hour, commensurate with education and experience. To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before October 25, 2026. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2822 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: University Programs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations; auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2821?c=isu": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, School Psychology Program (3341)",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor, School Psychology Program (3341) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant or Associate Professor, School Psychology Program (3341) United States | req2821 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/17/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Assistant or Associate Professor, School Psychology Program (3341) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Open until filled Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description Idaho State University school psychology program is the only school psychology program in Idaho. Thus, school psychology faculty are instrumental in shaping the practice of school psychology in Idaho. This position will have teaching, research and scholarship, and service responsibilities in the Master and Educational Specialist programs in School Psychology. This position also participates in advising, recruiting and other student and College support functions. The successful candidate will teach three courses per semester including practicum seminar/supervision, research/scholarship, and service responsibilities (e.g., supporting candidates’ portfolio development and defense) in the School Psychology Program. Also, he or she will participate in advising, recruiting, and performing other college support functions. Due to an ongoing multiple year grant, there is potential for summer and grant related work. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities The successful candidate will teach three (3) courses per semester including practicum seminar/supervision, research/scholarship, and service responsibilities (e.g., supporting candidates’ portfolio development and defense) in the School Psychology Program. Also, he or she will participate in advising, recruiting, and performing other college support functions. Minimum Qualifications - Earned doctorate in School Psychology or related field (ABD will be considered) - Ability to teach school psychology courses - Ability to advise graduate students and guide student research projects - Strong written and verbal skills - A record of scholarly accomplishment commensurate with levels Preferred Qualifications -Experience teaching school psychology related courses (e.g., psycho-diagnosis, legal and ethical issues in school psychology, consultation in schools, practicum in school psychology) -Advise graduate students and guide student research projects -Experience teaching in on-line, distance, or virtual environments -Content-area certification -Record of scholarly productivity and grant submission/grant work Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled . Salary will be between $66,000 - $69,000 at the Assistant Professor level and $69,000 -$73,000 at the Associate Professor level, per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2821 Type: Working 9 months per year Position: Faculty Tenure Track Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2819?c=isu": {
      "title": "Advisor/Planner, Educational Talent Search, TRIO Student Services (2552)",
      "description": "Advisor/Planner, Educational Talent Search, TRIO Student Services (2552) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Advisor/Planner, Educational Talent Search, TRIO Student Services (2552) United States | req2819 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/17/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Advisor/Planner, Educational Talent Search, TRIO Student Services (2552) Twin Falls NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: October 18, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description This position is located at the Twin Falls outreach campus serving 300 high school students. The successful candidates will establish, coordinate and conduct activities to inform low-income, first-generation persons about available financial aid and post-secondary education opportunities; to assist individuals in selecting, applying for and gaining financial assistance in enrolling in programs of post-secondary education. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Recruitment and Documentation (40% time spent) -Responsible for recruitment of potential participants and securing appropriate documentation for client eligibility (responsible for ensuring that 2/3rd of students are both 1st generation to college and meet federal income guidelines). -Maintaining accurate and confidential records for 250 students (including college and career plans, transcripts, test scores, scholarships, GPA, events attended, etc.). -Ongoing review of student caseload including: student progress as it relates to needs assessment and learning plan, documentation of students who have moved or left the program, scholarships received, financial aid received, etc. Maintain student files with all necessary physical documentation to ensure compliance with federal requirements. Academic Advising & Planning (60% time spent) -Provide academic assistance at target schools at least weekly, such as class selection for both secondary and postsecondary, study skills, goal setting, time management, academic success, career interest inventories, and technology. -Develop and maintain working and trusting relationships with participants while ensuring program services are provided as outlined in the federal grant. -Provide information to students regarding post-secondary opportunities including admissions, financial aid (FAFSA), scholarships, ACT/SAT/COMPASS testing, and course selection, CIS, Internet college searches, scholarship searches. Minimum Qualifications -Bachelor's\ndegree in\neducation, counseling, student personnel, or another related area,  (in lieu of a Bachelor’s Degree, a minimum of six years combined education, training, and experience may be considered). -Experience working\nwith underrepresented students & high school students. -Excellent\ninterpersonal and communication skills. -Must have\naccess to and use of own transportation. Preferred Qualifications -Master's\ndegree in an academic discipline, education, student personnel, counseling, or\nrelated area. -Knowledge of\ntarget area (Southcentral Idaho). -Knowledge of\nrecruitment strategies for limited-income and first-generation students. -Experience\nwith state or federal record keeping. -Bilingual in\nEnglish and Spanish. -Experience\nand knowledge of Federal TRIO programs. -Preferred candidates will have personal, socioeconomic, cultural, or\nacademic backgrounds that align closely with the target communities served. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 18, 2026 . Salary will be $45,605 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2819 Type: Working 11 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2820?c=isu": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant, General Counsel (1157)",
      "description": "Executive Assistant, General Counsel (1157) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Executive Assistant, General Counsel (1157) United States | req2820 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/16/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Executive Assistant, General Counsel (1157) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: October 18, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Executive Assistant to the General Counsel provides high-level administrative and executive support to the Office of the General Counsel and serves as a trusted administrative partner to the General Counsel.  The position is responsible for coordinating schedules, meetings, communications, travel, and other administrative activities necessary to support the operations of the department.  The Executive Assistant works with a high degree of professionalism, discretion, confidentiality, and independent judgement due to the sensitive legal and institutional matters handled by the office. The successful candidate will be highly organized, responsive, detail-oriented, and able to anticipate needs and manage competing priorities in a fast paced environment.  The Executive Assistant interacts regularly with University leadership, faculty, staff, and internal and external stakeholders. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities -Legal Operations. -Provide executive-level administrative support to the General Counsel, including calendar management, meeting coordination, travel, correspondence, and preparation of meeting materials. -Coordinate meetings and activities involving the General Counsel, University leadership, attorneys, external counsel, and other stakeholders. -Prepare, organize, and maintain agendas, briefing materials, reports, correspondence, presentations, records, and other documents. -Receive, prioritize, and appropriately route inquiries and communications directed to the Office of the General Counsel. -Coordinate administrative aspects of legal, litigation, subpoena, and other sensitive matters as directed by the General Counsel or attorneys within the Office. -Process invoices, travel authorizations, expense reimbursements, purchasing documentation, and other administrative transactions in accordance with University policies. -Maintain confidential files, records, and other information systems for the Office. -Assist with coordination of Office projects, training, events, and other initiatives, including tracking timelines, action items, and follow-up. -Maintain professional relationships with internal and external stakeholders and exercise appropriate judgment when handling sensitive information. -May provide work direction to student employees as assigned. -Perform other reasonable duties as assigned by the General Counsel. Minimum Qualifications -Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution or an equivalent combination of education and related experience. -At least five (5) years of progressively responsible administrative or executive support experience. -Demonstrated ability to organize, prioritize, and coordinate complex schedules, meetings, and administrative activities. -Demonstrated ability to exercise independent judgment, initiative, discretion, and confidentiality. -Excellent organizational, interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. -Strong computer skills, including proficiency with Google Workspace, and the ability to learn new programs and software. -Ability to work independently and effectively under pressure while maintaining a highly professional demeanor. Preferred Qualifications -Experience providing executive support in higher education or another complex organization. -Experience working in a legal, compliance, governmental, or similarly confidential environment. -Experience supporting senior leadership and coordinating complex meetings, projects, or institutional activities. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 18, 2026 . Salary will be between $60,000 and $65,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2820 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: General Counsel Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2817?c=isu": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Mechanical and Measurement & Control Engineering (8070)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Mechanical and Measurement & Control Engineering (8070) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor, Mechanical and Measurement & Control Engineering (8070) United States | req2817 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/14/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Assistant Professor, Mechanical and Measurement & Control Engineering (8070) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Open until filled Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description Idaho State University’s Department of Mechanical and Measurement & Control Engineering (MMCE) invites applications to join our dynamic and growing team. The position is for a 9-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Energy and Power Systems starting August 2027 until filled. As an Assistant Professor in MMCE, the expectations for the successful applicant are to participate in developing and teaching both undergraduate and graduate mechanical engineering courses, as well as in the core undergraduate curriculum, to build a collaborative, externally funded research program and to perform professional service. Consideration will be given to applicants with broad research interests in Energy systems which include conventional, emerging, and sustainable technologies to expand and complement our current research endeavors. To aid in these endeavors, the candidate is expected to participate synergistically with MMCE faculty in the activities of the Engineering Research Center (ERC), other research activities in the College of Science and Engineering (CoSE), across campus, and with external collaborators such as researchers at the nearby Idaho National Laboratory (INL). This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities • Teaching a broad set of undergraduate/graduate courses across the Mechanical Engineering curriculum. Courses may be offered via distance learning to the Idaho Falls and Twin Falls campuses. •    Pursue and establish an active, collaborative, externally funded research program, including publication of research, participation at conferences, and supporting undergraduate and graduate students. •    Undergraduate/graduate student recruitment and academic advising. •    Must be willing and capable to building synergistic interactions both within the department, and across campus. •    Mentoring undergraduate and graduate students in research projects. •    Perform professional and university (department, college, and university) service. •    Mentoring undergraduate student projects and clubs. Minimum Qualifications •  An earned Bachelor and Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering or equivalent are required.  ABD with completion by time of appointment may be considered. •    Strong interest in undergraduate and graduate teaching. •    Demonstrated record of research (publications and/or seeking external funding). •    Obtain an Idaho Professional Engineering (P.E.) license within three years. •    Demonstrated excellent verbal and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications •    Demonstrated excellence in teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses in mechanical engineering. •    Demonstrated commitment to building collaborative partnerships and establishing externally funded research program with mechanical engineering faculty. •    Research that expands and complements our current endeavors. •    Demonstrated potential for establishing research collaborations with external partners such as INL, other national labs and industries in the area of energy systems. •    Involvement with student groups and organizations. •    Evidence of course or program assessment (Accreditation Board for Engineering and Technology, ABET). •    Industry experience and/or post-doctoral experience. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled . Salary will be between $85,000 and $90,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2817 Type: Working 9 months per year Position: Faculty Tenure Track Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2816?c=isu": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor, Computer Aided Design Drafting, COT (7575)",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor, Computer Aided Design Drafting, COT (7575) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Clinical Instructor, Computer Aided Design Drafting, COT (7575) United States | req2816 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/10/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Clinical Instructor, Computer Aided Design Drafting, COT (7575) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Open until filled Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To provide quality experience-based instruction to Computer Aided Design Drafting students in both classroom and laboratory environments. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered Key Responsibilities 1. Deliver quality, experience-based instruction and hands-on laboratory activities designed to prepare students for successful entry into the workforce (70%) 2. Collaboratively work with program faculty, the Department Chair, and Technical Advisory Committee members to develop and maintain program curriculum (8%) 3. Recruit and advise Computer-Aided Design Drafting students (5%) 4. Participate in professional development activities to maintain state certification and engage in lifelong learning (5%) 5. Collaboratively work with program and departmental faculty to continuously assess and improve the program to maintain accreditation.  This will include participating in meetings to discuss and assess the program, and developing reports to maintain program accreditation. (5%) 6. Actively participate in departmental, college, university, and community professional service opportunities (5%) 7. Develop and maintain quality relationships with business/industry and other employers (2%) Minimum Qualifications • Associate’s degree in Computer-Aided Drafting, or closely related area of study, and 12,000 hours of full-time, successful, recent, gainful employment in a Computer-Aided Drafting related occupation OR a bachelor’s degree in Computer-Aided Drafting, or closely related area of study, and 6,000 hours of full-time, successful, recent, gainful employment in a Computer Aided Drafting related occupation • Postsecondary Occupational Specialist Certification from the Idaho Division of Career & Technical Education or meet the requirements to obtain such certification • Ability to effectively communicate in both written and oral forms • Strong interpersonal and presentation skills • Ability to operate a computer efficiently and use word processing software, email, and internet browsers • Proficiency in use of AutoCAD software • Proficiency in applied algebra, geometry, and trigonometry Preferred Qualifications • At least 16,000 hours of full-time, successful, recent, gainful employment in a Computer-Aided Drafting-related occupation • Experience with Geometric Dimensioning and Tolerancing • Experience using Revit software • Experience using Autodesk Inventor software • Experience teaching/training others in a professional or educational setting • Demonstrated efforts to stay current with an evolving industry through training or self-study in the operation of new equipment, software, and methods • Hold current professional certifications related to Design Drafting Additional Information Y ou must submit the following to be considered: CV/resume C over letter A list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information A professional portfolio containing 3-5 drawings. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled . Salary will be between $55,000 - $65,000 (up to $70,000 available for candidates proficient in Autodesk Revit) per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2816 Type: Working 9 months per year Position: Faculty Non-Tenure Track Division: College of Technology Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
