    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2814?c=isu": {
      "title": "University Ombuds, President's Office (2846)",
      "description": "University Ombuds, President's Office (2846) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) University Ombuds, President's Office (2846) United States | req2814 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/8/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . University Ombuds, President's Office (2846) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: October 8, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description Reporting to the President, the\nUniversity Ombuds serves as a confidential, independent, impartial, and\ninformal resource for faculty and staff to address concerns, resolve conflicts,\nand promote fair treatment across the university. The Ombuds provides guidance\non university policies and procedures, facilitates communication, and assists\nin problem-solving while upholding principles of neutrality, confidentiality,\nand informality. The Ombuds does not advocate for\nindividuals but rather for fairness and impartial processes. The role serves as\nan alternative, informal channel for conflict resolution, separate from formal\nuniversity procedures. The Ombuds also identifies systemic trends and offers\nrecommendations to improve university policies and practices. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered Key Responsibilities Confidential\n     & Informal Conflict Resolution Support Provides a safe, confidential space for individuals to discuss concerns, explore options, and seek resolution strategies. Assists in informal dispute resolution through facilitated dialogue, conflict coaching, mediation, and shuttle diplomacy. Helps individuals understand university policies, procedures, and available resources without engaging in formal processes. Collaborates with Faculty/Staff Ombuds to provide mentorship and guidance, without formal oversight, related to the operationalization of International Ombuds Association (IOA) principles Impartiality\n     & Fair Process Advocacy Maintains neutrality and impartiality, ensuring fairness and objective treatment for all university members. Does not take sides, make decisions, or determine policy but instead promotes fair and ethical practices. Identifies patterns of systemic concerns and provides feedback to university leadership while preserving confidentiality. Independence\n     & Structural Autonomy Operates independently from university administration, reporting trends and recommendations without being part of formal processes. Has direct access to the President while maintaining functional independence. Does not participate in formal investigations, adjudications, or compliance-related functions in any capacity. Data\n     Collection & Reporting on Systemic Issues Tracks non-identifiable trends to identify recurring issues affecting the university community. Prepares annual reports with aggregated data and recommendations to enhance fairness and institutional effectiveness. Maintains records in accordance with IOA best practices, ensuring no permanent documentation of confidential discussions. Minimum Qualifications ●Master’s degree in conflict resolution, law, psychology, social work, organizational leadership, higher education administration, or a related field. ●Demonstrated professional experience in mediation, alternative dispute resolution (ADR), conflict coaching, or ombuds practice. ●Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to foster trust, neutrality, and confidentiality. ●Understanding of IOA Standards of Practice & Code of Ethics and commitment to its principles. Preferred Qualifications ●Professional certification in conflict resolution or mediation and/or prior ombuds experience. ●Experience working in higher education, complex environments and highly emotional situations settings. ●Experience in higher education or working directly with faculty. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 8, 2026 . Salary will be between $70,000 - $75,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2814 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Presidents Office Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2812?c=isu": {
      "title": "Systems & Process Improvement Analyst (2924)",
      "description": "Systems & Process Improvement Analyst (2924) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Systems & Process Improvement Analyst (2924) United States | req2812 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/1/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Systems & Process Improvement Analyst (2924) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: October 25, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Systems & Process Improvement Analyst provides analytical, facilitation, documentation, and implementation support for university-wide process improvement initiatives. Working within the Innovation Hub’s Systems & Process Improvement Center, the Analyst partners with faculty, staff, administrators, subject matter experts, project teams, and technology partners to understand how work is currently performed, identify opportunities for improvement, develop future-state processes, and support implementation of sustainable solutions. The position applies systems thinking, process analysis, data analysis, and continuous improvement methods to institutional operations. The Analyst examines the relationships among people, processes, policies, technology, data, organizational structures, and user experience to identify root causes and develop practical improvements. The position expands the University’s capacity to conduct systems and process improvement work. It operates under the strategic and methodological leadership of the Director of Systems & Process Improvement and works collaboratively with Innovation Hub project management, workplace training, change leadership, and technology partners. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Analyze current-state processes: Assess institutional processes, services, workflows, and business practices; engage stakeholders and subject matter experts to understand how work is performed; and document processes, handoffs, decision points, dependencies, variations, and areas of inefficiency. Identify improvement opportunities: Conduct root-cause analysis and apply process improvement, Lean, systems-thinking, and problem-solving methods to identify opportunities to simplify, standardize, consolidate, automate, redesign, or eliminate work. Design future-state solutions: Collaborate with stakeholders to develop improved processes, workflows, roles, responsibilities, controls, service models, and documentation; evaluate alternatives based on effectiveness, efficiency, feasibility, risk, cost, user experience, and institutional impact. Conduct business and systems analysis: Gather and document business and functional requirements; analyze relationships among processes, systems, data, policies, organizational structures, and users; and identify technology dependencies, manual work, duplicate data entry, and opportunities for automation. Support implementation and adoption: Translate recommendations into actionable implementation plans and support pilots, testing, rollout, and post-implementation review. Partner with project management, technology, training, and change leadership resources to support successful adoption of improvements. Measure and evaluate results: Gather and analyze qualitative and quantitative data, establish baselines and performance measures, evaluate outcomes, and use findings and stakeholder feedback to determine whether improvements are achieving intended results. Develop and maintain documentation: Create and maintain process maps, workflow diagrams, requirements, standard operating procedures, process guides, recommendations, analytical summaries, and other materials needed to communicate and sustain improvements. Contribute to institutional improvement capacity: Develop and support repeatable tools, methodologies, and resources that strengthen the University’s overall capacity for systems and process improvement. Minimum Qualifications ● Bachelor’s degree in business administration, operations, organizational development, public administration, information systems, data analytics, industrial or systems disciplines, or a related field; or an equivalent combination of relevant education and professional experience. ● At least one (1) year experience analyzing processes, workflows, systems, operations, data, or organizational problems. ● At least one (1) year experience gathering, organizing, analyzing, and synthesizing information to support problem-solving or decision-making. ● At least one (1) year experience documenting processes, workflows, requirements, procedures, or other complex information. ● At least one (1) year experience working collaboratively on projects, initiatives, or operational improvements involving multiple stakeholders or functional areas. Preferred Qualifications ● Three (3) years experience in higher education, government, healthcare, or another complex or decentralized organization. ● Three (3) years experience with Lean, Lean Six Sigma, continuous improvement, business process management, systems thinking, business analysis, or related methodologies. ● Three (3) years experience developing process maps, workflow documentation, business requirements, or other process-analysis deliverables. ● Three (3) years experience supporting technology implementations, workflow automation, system redesign, or other operational change initiatives. ● Three (3) years experience analyzing operational, performance, or organizational data to identify trends, opportunities, or areas for improvement. ● Three (3) years experience facilitating or supporting cross-functional projects, interviews, workshops, process discovery sessions, or implementation activities. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 25, 2026 . Salary will be between $55,000 - $65,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2812 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Finance and Administration Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2809?c=isu": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor or Tenure Track Assistant Professor, Audiology (2923)",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor or Tenure Track Assistant Professor, Audiology (2923) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Clinical Assistant Professor or Tenure Track Assistant Professor, Audiology (2923) United States | req2809 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/1/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Clinical Assistant Professor or Tenure Track Assistant Professor, Audiology (2923) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: October 1, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Department of Communication Sciences & Disorders at Idaho State University is seeking an outstanding faculty member to join a dynamic, cohesive, and student-centered Audiology Program. To find the best fit for the program, this position is open track (Tenure Track or Clinical). A successful candidate would have the capacity and commitment to contribute to varying degrees across a broad array of areas including classroom instruction, student supervision and clinical instruction, and engagement in scholarly and service activities. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Clinical Track: - Develop and deliver undergraduate and graduate-level courses in audiology, covering key topics such as audiological assessment, hearing disorders, auditory rehabilitation, and hearing aid technology. - Supervise and mentor graduate audiology students in clinical settings, guiding them in assessing, diagnosing, and treating hearing and balance disorders. - Participate in department, college, and university committees, contributing to governance and decision-making processes. - Participate in creative and scholarly activities, including student mentoring of capstone projects. Tenure Track: - Develop and deliver undergraduate and graduate-level courses in audiology, covering key topics such as audiological assessment, hearing disorders, auditory rehabilitation, and hearing aid technology. - Participate in clinical teaching/clinical supervision and/or direct services to patients in the ISU Audiology Clinic. - Engage in scholarly activities that contribute to the field of audiology, such as research, publications, presentations, and grant writing. - Collaborate with colleagues on research projects and participate in professional conferences to disseminate findings. - Mentor graduate students in their research endeavors/capstone projects, providing guidance on project development, data analysis, and dissemination of results. - Provide service to the department, university, and profession. Minimum Qualifications Clinical Track: - Earned master's degree (e.g., MS, MA) and/or doctoral degree in Audiology (e.g., AuD, PhD). - Have a minimum of one (post-graduation) of clinical audiology experience. - Capacity and commitment to contribute to clinical teaching/clinical supervision. - Excellent interpersonal and professional skills and potential for excellence in didactic and clinical instruction. - Evidence of strong collaboration and interpersonal skills. - Be eligible for and obtain the American Speech/Language Hearing Association (ASHA) Certificate of Clinical Competence in Audiology (CCC-A); the successful candidate will need to be in the process of obtaining or have obtained the ASHA CCC-A at the time of hire. - Be eligible for and obtain Idaho audiology licensure; the successful candidate will need to be in the process of obtaining or have obtained an Idaho audiology license at the time of hire. Tenure Track: - Earned PhD in in Audiology, Speech and Hearing Sciences or research doctoral degree in a related field. - Candidate near completion of the doctorate (ABD) may be considered, but completion of the degree will be required to maintain employment. - Capacity and commitment to contribute to clinical teaching/clinical supervision. - Excellent interpersonal and professional skills and potential for excellence in didactic and clinical instruction. - Evidence of strong collaboration and interpersonal skills. - Be eligible for and obtain the American Speech/Language Hearing Association (ASHA) Certificate of Clinical Competence in. Audiology (CCC-A); the successful candidate will need to be in the process of obtaining or have obtained the ASHA CCC-A at the time of hire. - Be eligible for and obtain Idaho audiology licensure; the successful candidate will need to be in the process of obtaining or have obtained an Idaho audiology license at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications Clinical Track: - Experience teaching at the university level. - Experience supervising and instructing graduate students in a clinical environment. - Three years of hearing-aid experience with multiple product lines and manufacturers. - Demonstrated success in clinical and classroom teaching and research/ scholarly activities. - Interest in and/or experience in business administration and/or private practice clinical activities. - Other areas of preferred experience/interest include implantable devices (especially with cochlear implants), electrophysiological evaluation, and vestibular assessment and management. - Several years of university experience with a strong record of clinical instruction and involvement in creative and scholarly activities would be required for the Associate Professor rank. Tenure Track: - Experience teaching at the university level. - Experience supervising and instructing graduate students in a clinical environment. - Experiences with and/or capacity to participate in providing hearing aid services. - Demonstrated success in grant writing and research (a variety of specialty areas will be considered). - Other areas of preferred experience/interest include experience with or a desire to learn implantable devices (especially cochlear implants), electrophysiological evaluation, and vestibular assessment and management. - Several years of university experience (e.g., full time or adjunct) with a strong record of scholarship and grant writing would be required for the Associate Professor rank. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 1, 2026 . Salary will be between $85,000 and $90,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2809 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Faculty Non-Tenure Track Division: Kasiska Division of Health Sciences Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2792?c=isu": {
      "title": "Curator/Assistant Professor, Idaho Museum of Natural History & Biological Sciences (3756)",
      "description": "Curator/Assistant Professor, Idaho Museum of Natural History & Biological Sciences (3756) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Curator/Assistant Professor, Idaho Museum of Natural History & Biological Sciences (3756) United States | req2792 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/1/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Curator/Assistant Professor, Idaho Museum of Natural History & Biological Sciences (3756) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: October 30, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Idaho Museum of Natural History and the Department of Biological Sciences at Idaho State University invite applications for a joint-appointed Museum Curator/tenure-track Assistant Professor in Vertebrate Paleontology to begin August 2027. IMNH and ISU share a common mission to provide and nurture opportunities for understanding living systems through high-quality public education, scientific discovery, and service.  The successful candidate will have a doctorate in the biological or earth sciences with substantial, documented experience and training in vertebrate paleontology and collections management. Postdoctoral experience is preferred. Startup funds are available. IMNH is the official natural history museum for Idaho and has 10 staff members, employs dozens of student internships, and cares for over 1.5M specimens in life, earth, and anthropological sciences. The Earth Science collection includes a Federal repository with existing strengths in Miocene to Pleistocene mammals. The Department of Biological Sciences has over 25 faculty members specializing in sub-disciplines of the biological sciences and serves over 500 undergraduate majors and over 40 graduate students. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities The joint appointment workload is structured 2/3 time for the IMNH and 1/3 time for the Department of Biological Sciences. Duties comprise research, curation, teaching, and service. The successful candidate will be expected to provide curatorial oversight of the Earth Sciences Division and vertebrate collections of the Life Sciences Division. This role includes developing a vision and direction for growth, increasing student and public engagement, and creative integration of these collections with other branches of the Museum and associated functions (e.g., Idaho Virtualization Lab). Research specialty is open, with preference for candidates whose research addresses large-scale questions, is rooted in field- and specimen-based evidence, and holds potential to build collections at the Museum. They will provide content expertise for Museum programming, public lectures, and exhibits. In the Biological Sciences Department, the successful candidate will be expected to build a collaborative, interdisciplinary, and extramurally funded research program in vertebrate paleontology that involves mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Teaching responsibilities for this position will include vertebrate paleontology, comparative vertebrate anatomy, seminars and other courses in the candidate’s area of expertise or in core curriculum. The Museum and the Department of Biological Sciences have a high expectation for collegiality and shared responsibility to meet institutional vision and goals. Minimum Qualifications 1.    PhD in Biology, Geology or related discipline by August 2027. 2.    Experience in Museum Collections Management. 3.    Evidence of teaching experience. 4.    Demonstrated scholarship in paleontological research. Preferred Qualifications 1.    Postdoctoral experience. 2.    More than 2 years of Collections Management or Curator experience. 3.    Demonstrated success in attracting extramural research funding. 4.    Evidence of public engagement. 5.    Experience working within a highly collaborative and interdisciplinary environment. 6.    Demonstrated success in recruiting and working with students. 7.    Experience in Intermountain West paleontology. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 30, 2026 . Salary will be $68,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2792 Type: Working 9 months per year Position: Faculty Tenure Track Division: Idaho Museum Natural History Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2805?c=isu": {
      "title": "Accounting Manager, ISU Foundation (2922)",
      "description": "Accounting Manager, ISU Foundation (2922) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Accounting Manager, ISU Foundation (2922) United States | req2805 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Accounting Manager, ISU Foundation (2922) Pocatello - Main Eligible for a hybrid remote work schedule, as approved by the hiring manager Priority Date: October 9, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The ISU Foundation serves as the fundraising and advancement partner of Idaho State University, securing and stewarding private support that strengthens the University’s mission and impact. The Foundation is committed to fostering a culture defined by empowerment, appreciation, engagement, and accountability, cornerstones that guide how we work, collaborate, and celebrate success. Our team values trust and shared purpose as we build a strategic and sustainable advancement organization. Together, we cultivate relationships that connect donors, alumni, and partners to the transformative work taking place across the University. Idaho State University and the ISU Foundation are actively planning a historic and ambitious comprehensive fundraising campaign. The Idaho State University Foundation is seeking a positive, energetic, and experienced Accounting Manager to join its team. Reporting directly to the Chief Financial Officer (CFO), the Accounting Manager plays a critical role in managing daily finance and accounting operations while ensuring accuracy, integrity, and compliance of financial information. This position is responsible for a broad range of accounting functions, including general ledger management, journal entries, accounts payable and receivable, financial reporting,  month-end and year-end close, audit and tax preparation, compliance, and financial analysis. The ideal candidate will possess a strong understanding of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), demonstrate exceptional attention to detail, and have the ability to manage competing priorities in a dynamic environment. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Ensure accurate and timely recording of daily financial transactions, including accounts payable, accounts receivable, credit card transactions, cash receipts, and other financial activity. Perform general ledger functions, including preparation and posting of journal entries, balance sheet reconciliations, and maintenance of accounting schedules. Conduct monthly reconciliations of bank accounts, investment funds, along with daily reconciliation of banking transactions. Prepare monthly, quarterly, and annual financial reports, including financial statements, trial balance, balance sheet, cash flow reports, and other management reports. Manage monthly and year-end financial close, including journal entries, accruals, reconciliations, account maintenance, and preparation of supporting documentation. Monitor cash and investment balances and assist the CFO with cash flow forecasting and financial planning. Ensure financial transactions comply with (GAAP), applicable state and federal regulations, and organizational policies and procedures. Assist the CFO and Chief Executive Officer (CEO) with budget development, monitoring, forecasting and analysis. Ensure accurate tracking and recording of revenues and expenses by account, program, and funding source. Communicate regularly with the CFO regarding financial activity trends, issues, and recommendations. Research, investigate, and resolve discrepancies related to payments, accounts, and financial transactions; prepare corrective journal entries as needed. Prepare documentation and schedules required for annual financial reporting, tax filings, and external audits; collaborate with auditors as needed. Provide financial support and reporting assistance to Board committees, including Finance, Investment, and Audit Committees. Provide fiscal support to staff, donors, university employees, and fund administrators. Identify opportunities for process improvement and contribute to the development and implementation of financial policies and procedures. Supervise finance technician, interns, and/or student employees as assigned. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned. Required Skills and Competencies: - Strong critical thinking and problem solving skills. - Excellent analytical skills with the ability to interpret and communicate financial information. - Exceptional attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. - Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. - Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with internal and external stakeholders. - Strong written and verbal communication skills. - Ability to exercise sound judgement and maintain confidentiality. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in accounting, finance, business administration, or a related field. Minimum of three years progressive accounting experience. Proficiency with financial management systems and accounting software. Demonstrated ability to perform financial analysis, problem-solving, and decision-making. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with individuals at all levels. Ability to manage multiple responsibilities, prioritize workload, and meet established deadlines. Prior supervisory or team leadership experience. Preferred Qualifications Certified Public Accountant (CPA) designation. Experience with Financial Edge NXT, or similar nonprofit accounting/ERP systems. Experience in higher education, nonprofit organizations, or fund accounting. Experience with investment accounting, donor-restricted funds, and nonprofit financial reporting. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 9, 2026 . Salary will be between $60,000 - $70,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2805 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: University Advancement Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2803?c=isu": {
      "title": "Recruitment Systems Analyst, Admissions (2919)",
      "description": "Recruitment Systems Analyst, Admissions (2919) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Recruitment Systems Analyst, Admissions (2919) United States | req2803 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Recruitment Systems Analyst, Admissions (2919) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: September 24, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Recruitment Systems Analyst supports the technical, operational, and data-management functions that drive Idaho State University’s recruitment and admissions processes. Reporting to the Director of Data Analytics and Recruitment Strategy, this position manages day-to-day CRM operations (Slate CRM and Ellucian Recruit CRM during transition), ensures data accuracy across recruitment systems, executes workflow and communication logic, and provides reporting and troubleshooting support for staff. The Analyst plays a key role in maintaining clean, reliable data; supporting recruitment and communication strategies; and ensuring that Admissions & Recruitment staff are able to use CRM tools effectively and efficiently. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered Key Responsibilities Manage day-to-day CRM operations and workflow execution • Support daily operations within the CRM, including workflow execution, data imports, event setup, query management, and user task queues • Build, test, and maintain forms, automations, workflows, rules, and population logic as directed by the Director of Data Analytics and Recruitment Strategy • Update and maintain communication flows, including emails, text messages, and trigger logic • Troubleshoot CRM issues, respond to user requests, and ensure timely resolution of errors, duplicate records, and workflow interruptions • Assist with the configuration, testing, and rollout of new CRM features and enhancements. Ensure data integrity, accuracy, and compliance • Perform routine data validation, de-duplication, quality checks, and record maintenance within CRM systems • Support accurate data flow between Slate CRM, Banner, and other university systems • Maintain documentation of data standards, workflow steps, and system rules to ensure consistency across users • Ensure compliance with FERPA and university data security requirements for all recruitment-related data Provide reporting, analytics support, and system documentation • Create, update, and maintain operational reports and queries to support recruitment staff, marketing efforts, events, and admissions operations • Assist in generating dashboards, tracking documents, and metric summaries used by leadership to evaluate funnel progress and recruitment outcomes • Prepare documentation, job aids, and reference materials for CRM processes and updates • Work with the Director to evaluate system performance, identify process improvements, and streamline workflows Support user training and functional support across departments • Serve as a primary point of contact for CRM users needing training, troubleshooting, or help understanding workflows • Conduct user training sessions for new staff and ongoing refresher training as needed • Provide one-on-one support to staff members experiencing technical issues or needing assistance with CRM tools • Collaborate closely with recruitment, ambassadors, marketing, and admissions processing teams to ensure system needs are met Support Slate implementation and ongoing system development • Assist with integration testing, validation of new functionality, and documentation of new processes • Work with IT and the Director to maintain and optimize system integrations and API processes Minimum Qualifications 1.    Bachelor’s degree in Informatics, Information Systems, Business, Data Analytics, or a related field 2.    Experience working with CRM systems, databases, or other information systems 3.    Strong analytical and problem-solving skills 4.    Demonstrated ability to manage technical tasks with accuracy and attention to detail 5.    Proficiency with Excel, data tools, and basic reporting functions 6.    Strong interpersonal and communication skills 7.    Ability to learn new systems quickly and provide user support 8.    Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment Preferred Qualifications 1.    Experience with Slate CRM, Recruit CRM, Banner, Argos, Tableau or other higher-education systems 2.    Experience working in admissions, recruitment, or higher education operations 3.    Experience with SQL, reporting tools, or basic scripting 4.    Experience documenting processes or writing user tutorials Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before September 24, 2026 . Salary will be between $50,000 - $55,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2803 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Admissions Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2683?c=isu": {
      "title": "Lab Manager, Treasure Valley Anatomy & Physiology Lab (1704)",
      "description": "Lab Manager, Treasure Valley Anatomy & Physiology Lab (1704) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Lab Manager, Treasure Valley Anatomy & Physiology Lab (1704) United States | req2683 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Lab Manager, Treasure Valley Anatomy & Physiology Lab (1704) Meridian/Boise NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: October 7, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The  Treasure Valley Anatomy & Physiology Laboratories (TVAPL_ Lab Manager is responsible for overseeing the day-to-day operations of the ISU–Meridian Treasure Valley Anatomy & Physiology Laboratories (TVAPL) and ensuring a safe and effective laboratory environment that supports high-quality human anatomy education, research, and training. Key responsibilities include implementing the highest laboratory safety standards, policies, and procedures; managing the ethical procurement and disposition of human anatomical donors and specimens; actively participating in lab-based teaching and dissection; managing lab operational resources and expenditures; supporting budgeting and planning efforts; supervising staff, techs, and volunteers; and coordinating scheduling for bioskills and other professional laboratory programs. Working closely with the Director of the Labs, the Lab Manager also supports the continued expansion and strategic growth of TVAPL. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities •Oversee day-to-day operations of the ISU–Meridian TVAPL labs. •Ensure strict compliance with all laboratory safety, security, and regulatory requirements, including hazardous waste handling and disposal. •Implement and maintain guidelines, policies, and standard operating procedures governing lab use and operations. •Manage the ethical procurement, use, and disposition of human anatomical donors and fresh/frozen specimens to support TVAPL lab users, including ICOM. •Actively participate in TVAPL lab-based educational programs and courses through teaching and dissection. •Take active part in the development and execution of annual TVAPL budgets, business, and staffing plans. •Supervise collaboratively TVAPL staff, technicians, volunteers, and support personnel. •Manage laboratory financial expenditures, chemicals, consumables, equipment, and supplies. •Work with vendors to obtain bids, procure supplies and equipment, and recommend necessary purchases. •Schedule and oversee TVAPL Bioskills and professional lab activities. •Ensure effective execution of TVAPL's mission, goals, and strategic priorities. •Drive the strategic growth and expansion of the TVAPL labs. Minimum Qualifications •Master’s degree in human anatomy, biology, physiology, clinical laboratory science, exercise science, or related fields from a regionally accredited university in the USA or a USA recognized foreign university. •Minimum of three years relevant management experience in a lab-setting in higher education or health care environment that includes supervisory and budgetary experience. •Demonstrated understanding of compliance with regulations, organizational skills including setting priorities, and sound interpersonal and communication skills. •Demonstrated proficiency in human anatomical donor prosection, and comprehensive management of the anatomy laboratory facility. •Demonstrated high professional and ethical standards. Preferred Qualifications •Doctoral degree in human anatomy, biology, physiology, clinical laboratory science, exercise science, or related fields from a regionally accredited university in the USA or a USA recognized foreign university. •Record of success in teaching various lab-based human anatomy, clinical anatomy, and related instructional courses. •More than five years relevant management experience in a lab-setting in higher education or health care environment that includes supervisory and budgetary experience. •Demonstrated collaboration with multiple groups including medical personnel, faculty and medical, post-secondary, high school students, and community stakeholders. •At least two years of experience managing human anatomical laboratory work. •Experience with operations for human anatomical donations programming. •Demonstrated experience with grant writing and/or fundraising. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before October 7, 2026 . Salary will be between $75,000 and $80,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2683 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Kasiska Division of Health Sciences Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2664?c=isu": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Counseling (3736)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Counseling (3736) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor, Counseling (3736) United States | req2664 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/20/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Assistant Professor, Counseling (3736) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Open until filled Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description Teach core CACREP courses in the Masters and Ph.D programs. Advise Master and Ph.D students. Supervise practicum and internship students. Direct dissertations. Summit grants. Scholarly inquiry. University and professional service. This is for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor to coordinate the School Counseling Program. Anticipated start date will be August 2027. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered Key Responsibilities 1. Teach the school counseling courses. 2. Teach the core CACREP core classes at masters and doctoral level. 3. Assist in coordinating school counseling practicum and internship sites. 4. Consult with local and regional school districts on pupil personnel issues. 5. Ensure program quality via accreditation and certification 6. Engage in scholarly productivity. 7. Provide advisement at the masters and doctoral level. Minimum Qualifications Doctorate in counselor education from a CACREP accredited program earned no later than August 2027. Teaching and supervision experience. Evidence for scholarly productivity. Eligible for the Licensed Professional Counselor credential in Idaho. Preferred Qualifications Publication in the ACA family of journals relevant to school counseling. Involvement in national counseling associations, and those directly applicable to school counseling. Successful grant procurement. Experience as a school counseling program coordinator. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled . Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2664 Type: Working 9 months per year Position: Faculty Tenure Track Division: Division of Health Sciences Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Idaho State University is committed to access and reasonable accommodations, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact jobs@isu.edu. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
