    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2846?c=isu": {
      "title": "HVAC Specialist, Facilities Services (1851)",
      "description": "HVAC Specialist, Facilities Services (1851) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) HVAC Specialist, Facilities Services (1851) United States | req2846 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/15/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . HVAC Specialist, Facilities Services (1851) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To perform journey-level installation, maintenance, and repair of\nheating, ventilating, and air conditioning (HVAC) systems; perform related\nwork. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Examples of Duties 1. HVAC. -Analyzes, repairs, and performs preventive maintenance on all HVAC installations, fire and boiler alarm and surveillance control systems (high and low pressure). -Defines and implements preventive maintenance programs for motors, steam condensate return traps, pumps, controls, compressors, auxiliary heating and cooling systems, and related devices. -Compiles reports for changes to the HVAC system which includes reporting costs, estimating values, and justifying changes. -Reviews work of contractors' new and remodel construction for compliance to specifications and compatibility with existing HVAC systems. -Maintains air distribution and balance systems and heat exchange equipment. -Adds chemicals and analyzes water treatment for chill water and heating systems. -Plans and installs auxiliary control systems. -Lights off, shuts down, and operates boilers. -Prepares system for winter carry-over and cold weather conditions. -Calibrates pipe and vent sizes and BTUs required for installations. -May design and install sheet metal. -Installs/inspects thermostats, and electrical wiring of furnaces, unit heaters, and cooling units. -Reviews new designs and concepts of HVAC systems. -Operates microprocessor fan control and fire alarm systems. -Programs computerized energy management equipment. 2. Miscellaneous. -Tests/maintains emergency electrical equipment such as generators and battery-operated lighting. -Inspects and maintains specialized items such as clothes washers, dishwashers, coolers, freezers, ice machines, and domestic refrigerators. -Runs wire, installs outlet boxes, repairs switches and light fixtures. -Repairs broken pipes, fixes leaks, and cleans blocked pipes. -Assists other maintenance and crafts staff performing their duties. -Responds to emergency call-backs. Minimum Qualifications Experience: -Charging, starting,\nand checking for proper operation of HVAC type equipment and related devices. -Troubleshooting and repairing digital electronic and pneumatic HVAC control\nsystems. -Starting, stopping, and troubleshooting chiller operations and chilled water\nsystems. -Modifying and/or installing natural gas and water piping. -Operating, maintaining, diagnosing problems, and repairing industrial type\nHVAC systems and control devices. -Performing basic carpentry, plumbing, electrical, and sheet metal work. -Welding and repairing material and brazing pipe. -Cutting, brazing and soldering high pressure refrigerant piping. Supplemental\nInformation -This position\ninvolves lifting and carrying items weighing approximately 90 pounds, bending,\nstooping, and climbing ladders. Specialty\nRequirements -These positions at\nISU require the ability to demonstrate successful completion of both a physical\nexam, including cardiopulmonary function testing and chest x-ray, and a\nrespirator fit test. -These positions at ISU require a valid driver’s license. -These positions at ISU respond to emergency call backs. Additional Information I SU minimum for this classification is $21.25/hour, commensurate with education and experience. To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before October 29, 2026. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2846 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: OPERATIONS Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2844?c=isu": {
      "title": "Senior Accountant, Payroll (2788)",
      "description": "Senior Accountant, Payroll (2788) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Senior Accountant, Payroll (2788) United States | req2844 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/15/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Senior Accountant, Payroll (2788) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: November 15, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Payroll Accountant provides accounting, financial, and administrative support to Idaho State University’s payroll operations, including assisting the Payroll Manager with the processing of the biweekly payroll, and preparing and maintaining accurate records in compliance with federal, state, and local payroll and wage laws. This position is housed in the Office of Human Resources and reports directly to the AVP of Finance, with a dotted line report to the AVP of Human Resources. The Payroll Accountant will work closely on a day-to-day basis with the Payroll Manager, Personnel Technician for Payroll Processing, and the Benefits Coordinator. The Payroll Accountant and Payroll Manager will both be cross-trained to run payroll to ensure redundancy and flexibility, as needed, to support biweekly payroll operations. Because ISU payroll is processed on a bi-weekly basis, the Payroll Accountant position requires the ability to work a regular schedule consistent with the needs of the university and payroll cycle. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Payroll Administration Support: •    Works in conjunction with the University Controller, Payroll Manager, Personnel Technician for Payroll Processing and Senior Accountant in Finance to support the administration and processing of biweekly payroll •    Prepares and maintains accurate records and reports of payroll transactions; facilitates audits by pulling ad-hoc payroll reports (data analysis of salary transactions) •    Ensures compliance with federal, state, and local payroll, wage, and hour laws and best practices •    Process and advise on best practices for payroll/salary redistribution of funding sources Payroll Processing Support: •    Cross trains with the Payroll Manager to understand all operations associated with payroll processing and is occasionally responsible for running biweekly payroll •    Reconcile Payroll Vendor & Levy Checks •    Process Payroll JV’s •    Prepare the prior month calculation for Box 12 DD and collaborate with benefits coordinator as needed. •    Prepare file for ADP and reconcile state accounts for out-of-state tax compliance •    In collaboration with HR Associate and Personnel Technician, support processing of the Education Tax through review and audit of employees utilizing Employee credit benefit •    Manage and process employee tuition waivers each semester •    Completes routine daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly and annual tasks associated with payroll processing •    Supports projects and/or process improvement based on changes that impact Payroll and/or Benefits programs; as directed by the University Controller or Payroll Manager and in collaboration with other units at the University Minimum Qualifications •    Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field from an accredited institution OR six (6) years equivalent professional experience •    At least four (4) years experience in accounting, finance, or related field, with at least one (1) year direct experience working in payroll related functions •    Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills to interact effectively with leadership, faculty, and staff at all organizational levels •    Strong problem solving, financial analysis, and investigative research skills •    Excellent organizational, prioritization, and multi-tasking capabilities while maintaining close attention to detail in a dynamic and complex environment Preferred Qualifications •    Advanced degree in Finance, Accounting, or related field •    Accounting experience within higher education •    At least two (2) years direct experience in payroll accounting functions Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 15, 2026 . Salary will be between $62,000 and $68,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2844 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Finance and Administration Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2843?c=isu": {
      "title": "Business Operations Manager, ISU Health Center (1287)",
      "description": "Business Operations Manager, ISU Health Center (1287) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Business Operations Manager, ISU Health Center (1287) United States | req2843 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/15/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Business Operations Manager, ISU Health Center (1287) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: November 15, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The ISU Health Center (ISU HC) seeks a Business Operations Manager to oversee and manage the administrative and business operations of the ISU Health Center. The position ensures efficient, organized, and compliant operations that support high-quality patient care and the effective delivery of health services. As clinic operations evolve, the position may support the expansion and coordination of business operations across additional health clinics and services within the Kasiska Division of Health Sciences (KDHS). This position is 32  to 40 hours per week. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Administrative Oversight: 40% -Oversee daily clinic operations and maintain accurate patient records. -Manage billing, insurance, provider credentialing, and insurance contract coordination with the Clinics Director of Operations. -Collaborate with the CPC Business Operations Manager on revenue cycle activities, including insurance verification, authorizations, payments, charge reconciliation, accounts receivable, claims, and denials. -Oversee the Banner registration feed to verify student, faculty, and staff eligibility. -Collaborate with the Medical Director and ISU clinic management team to support existing operations, expand services, and develop processes for new clinics. -Support the enhancement and expansion of healthcare services for students, including student-athletes, in alignment with institutional priorities. Human Resources: 30% -Recruit, train, coach, and supervise administrative and support staff, including custodial personnel. -Develop staff schedules and ensure adequate staffing and provider coverage. -Conduct performance evaluations and provide feedback to support professional development. -Maintain the electronic health record (EHR) system and train new employees. -Financial, Budget, and Inventory Management: 10% -Manage clinic budgets, expenses, revenue monitoring, student fee proposals, and cost control. -Track and reconcile financial transactions and reports. -Manage inventory and coordinate ordering of medical supplies, vaccines, medications, office materials, and equipment. Communication and Coordination: 10% -Facilitate communication among healthcare providers, staff, and patients to support coordinated care. -Collaborate with campus partners, including Counseling and Mental Health, Athletics, Student Affairs, Human Resources, Finance, and Health Sciences. Quality Improvement: 10% -Identify opportunities to improve clinic operations, patient services, and efficiency. -Implement quality improvement initiatives to enhance patient care and operational effectiveness. Healthcare Compliance: 10% -Ensure compliance with OSHA and applicable state and federal healthcare regulations. -Collaborate with Information Technology Services (ITS) to maintain cybersecurity and HIPAA privacy protections. -Develop and update policies and procedures, communicate regulatory changes, and provide staff training on compliance requirements. Perform other reasonable duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications -At least bachelor’s degree in healthcare administration, business administration, finance or a related field from an accredited institution or six (6) years of clinical setting experience. -At least three (3) years of relevant experience in healthcare management or administration including performance management, staff development and conflict resolution. -Healthcare knowledge including a strong understanding of healthcare regulations, billing, and policies and procedures including HIPAA and CMS. -Strong leadership and management skills to lead teams, set strategic goals and manage budgets. Preferred Qualifications -Master’s degree, MBA or MHA preferred. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 15, 2026 . Salary will be between $73,000 and $80,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2843 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Kasiska Division of Health Sciences Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2845?c=isu": {
      "title": "Mechanical Systems Operator, Facilities Services (2243)",
      "description": "Mechanical Systems Operator, Facilities Services (2243) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Mechanical Systems Operator, Facilities Services (2243) United States | req2845 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Mechanical Systems Operator, Facilities Services (2243) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To\noperate and maintain high-pressure boilers, chillers, and related equipment;\nperform related work. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Examples of Duties 1.\nMechanical systems operation. -Inspects heating equipment: checks fans, valving and piping, gauges, sight glasses and indication lights. -Insures proper operation of feed and return water pumps, sump and chemical pumps, water softeners, internal and external boiler components, electrical systems, and burners. -Maintains burner firing and fuel ratio control. -Boiler operation: maintains water level, steam pressure, proper deaeration tank operation, rotation of water and chemical pumps, and start-up and shut-down of boilers. -Maintains fuel system components. -Regulates continuous blowdown, blowdown water columns, top and bottom drums, and wall water boxes. -Blows water tubes in boiler with high-pressure steam and soot blowers to remove carbon deposits. -Water treatment: mixes chemicals. -Tests water condition for dissolved solids, \"P\", \"M\", and \"O\", alkalinity, sulfite, and pH levels. -Regulates chemical feed. -Maintains chemical usage information, boiler performance logs, recorder charts, and gas usage data. -Repairs drains and tubes. -Takes flow readings of water loops and air velocities in ducts to balance HVAC systems. -Monitors building automation and fire control systems and makes computer commands to start and stop fans, pumps, and related devices. -Monitors/repairs geothermal pumps and production, and injection systems. -Maintains heat exchangers, sand traps, injection wells, check valves, and pneumatic and automatic piping systems. 2.\nMaintenance. -Performs preventive maintenance on heat plant system. -Overhauls boilers. -Descales and repairs steam traps and expansion joints. -Cleans, lubricates and adjusts valves. -Inspects pump controls and fans. -Cleans areas in and around heating plant. -Paints walls, tanks, and stairways. -Performs preventive maintenance checks on fire extinguishers and fire control systems. -Checks for leaks in steam and condensate lines. -Cleans and changes filters and air handler on air conditioners and swamp coolers. -Performs routine maintenance plumbing. -Assists other maintenance staff performing their duties. Minimum Qualifications Good knowledge of: -The firing, operation, and maintenance of high-pressure steam boilers, chillers, and related systems and equipment -Heat transfer as it relates to heat plant steam generation -High-pressure steam fitting Experience: -Detecting and repairing malfunctions in boiler and chiller equipment -Chemically treating water for proper conditioning -Operating, dismantling, and maintaining boilers, pumps, valves, air conditioners, chillers and related systems Specialty Requirements - These\npositions at ISU require the following: -Valid\ndriver's license. -Respond\nto emergency call-backs. -Successful\ncompletion of both a physical exam, including cardiopulmonary function testing\nand chest x-ray, as well as a respirator fit test. Supplemental\nInformation These positions involve lifting and carrying\nitems weighing approximately 90 pounds, working in a noisy environment,\nbending, stooping, and crawling in and around confined spaces. Additional Information ISU minimum for this classification is $17.25/hour, commensurate with education and experience. To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before October 29, 2026. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2845 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: Finance and Administration Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2842?c=isu": {
      "title": "Financial Analyst, Financial Reporting & Analysis (3070)",
      "description": "Financial Analyst, Financial Reporting & Analysis (3070) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Financial Analyst, Financial Reporting & Analysis (3070) United States | req2842 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Financial Analyst, Financial Reporting & Analysis (3070) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: November 15, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The successful candidate assists in the preparation and written presentation of the annual audited financial statements of Idaho State University to help ensure that internal and external financial results are timely, accurate, and in accordance with appropriate policies and regulations. The position is also responsible for assisting in the development, analysis, and written presentation of the quarterly financial reports submitted to the Audit Committee of the Idaho State Board of Education (SBOE), including participation in drafting narrative analysis and notes to the statements. Performs complex analysis, reconciliation and accounting transactions supporting cash/bank reconciliation. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities •    Performs complex analysis, reconciliation and accounting transactions related to cash/bank reconciliation including (but not limited to): Process and balance the daily interface between the student and finance module; Reconciliation of bank deposits with Cashier’s deposits including follow up and resolution of discrepancies; Bank Reconciliation. •     Works with Assistant Controller and other team members to create new and maintain existing financial reports, create and maintain process documentation, and assists with new and ongoing process improvement projects. •    Collaborates with the Assistant Controller and other senior business unit leaders to assist in development and preparation of the annual audited financial statements of Idaho State University. •     Assists the Assistant Controller in planning and coordinating the external audit process, including coordination of the fieldwork process and coordination with internal staff of all required audit material and support for the external auditors. •     Assists in interpretation and implementation of new accounting standards to ensure compliance with GAAP in financial reporting and internal control administration, research new regulations, and recommends and implements approved changes. •     Prepares audit schedules and reconciliations in support of external financial statements audit. •     Responsibilities include participating in the preparation and analysis of the quarterly financial reports submitted to the SBOE Audit Committee. •    Involved in financial reporting projects such as the financial sections of the annual IPEDs report, preparation of financial survey data, and responding to Freedom of Information requests. •     Works closely with individuals within and outside the finance department to coordinate financial reporting processes and provide timely customer service. •    Other financial accounting and reporting tasks as assigned. Minimum Qualifications •    At least a bachelor’s degree in accounting, finance, or a closely related field or equivalent combinations of relevant education and experience may be considered. •    At least two (2) years of professional experience in financial analysis, accounting, budgeting, or a related area. •     Experience analyzing financial data, identifying trends, and preparing financial reports. •     Working knowledge of accounting and budgeting principles. •    Proficiency with Microsoft Excel, including formulas, pivot tables, data filtering, and data analysis. •    Ability to interpret complex financial information and communicate findings clearly to both financial and non-financial audiences. •     Demonstrated attention to detail, accuracy, organization, and problem-solving ability. •     Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet established deadlines. Preferred Qualifications •    Experience working in higher education, government, or another complex public-sector organization. •    Knowledge of fund accounting, governmental accounting standards, or university budgeting practices. •    Experience with enterprise financial systems, such as Ellucian Banner, Workday, PeopleSoft, or a comparable ERP system. •    Experience with SQL, Power BI or other platforms for data analysis and report creation. •    Experience improving or automating financial processes and reports. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 15, 2026 . Salary will be between $60,000 and $65,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2842 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Finance and Administration Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2856?c=isu": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Clinical Prof/Director of the Center of Entrepreneurship & Economic Development",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Clinical Prof/Director of the Center of Entrepreneurship & Economic Development | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate Clinical Prof/Director of the Center of Entrepreneurship & Economic Development United States | req2856 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Assistant/Associate Clinical Prof/Director of the Center of Entrepreneurship & Economic Development Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: November 29, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description Idaho State University's College of Business (COB) seeks a full-time Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor of Management and Center for Entrepreneurship and Economic Development (CEED) Director in its Department of Marketing and Management starting August 2027.  This appointment is for a 9-month position with opportunity for advancement. The College of Business is accredited by the AACSB. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Teach Management classes as needed at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with primary teaching duties in the area of Introduction to business/entrepreneurship, entrepreneurial Solutions (Senior Pitch course), and business planning. Conduct significant, relevant service to the department including overseeing  pitch competitions for regional high school students, students in the freshmen level introduction to Business course, and the university wide senior level pitch competition, as well as creating and growing other entrepreneurship events and competitions associated with the ISU COB, and working with external stakeholders to build and grow entrepreneurship programs. Provide academic and career advising to students and contribute to the advancement of the College and University. Minimum Qualifications At least a Master’s degree in Business, Entrepreneurship, or a\nclosely related field (e.g., Marketing) from an accredited institution. Evidence of demonstrated or potential teaching effectiveness in Business Management/Entrepreneurship and a record of participation in and helping coordinate Academic Entrepreneurship competitions and initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Four years of experience teaching Business Management/Entrepreneurship courses along with evidence of teaching effectiveness in Business Management/Entrepreneurship courses and demonstrated effectiveness launching, operating, and/or coordinating Entrepreneurship Pitch Competitions, Business creation initiatives, and/or academic and outreach programs that support and develop entrepreneurs/new businesses. Other possible secondary areas of interest may include supply chain management/Operations management or healthcare management. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 29, 2026 . Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2856 Type: Working 9 months per year Position: Faculty Non-Tenure Track Division: College of Business Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2855?c=isu": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor (1596)",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor (1596) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Financial Aid Counselor (1596) United States | req2855 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Financial Aid Counselor (1596) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date:  November 29, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The Financial Aid Counselor provides support for and assists with the administration of Federal Financial Aid programs. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities -Verification\n     of financial aid applications including reviewing submitted documents to\n     confirm the accuracy of student data and resolving errors and/or\n     conflicting information. -Provide\n     financial aid counseling to student, parents and the university community\n     as needed through appointments, On-Call rotation, phone back-up rotation,\n     and presentations regarding the financial aid application process, student\n     eligibility, financial aid budget inquiries, and financial literacy. -Provides\n     customer service support, serving as an information resource for students,\n     parents and staff. -Assist\n     with the completion and trouble-shooting of issues with the Free\n     Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA). -Support\n     outreach efforts which may include high school or campus financial aid\n     workshops. -Determine\n     student eligibility for aid programs and revise aid packages as needed,\n     including review of NSLDS and/or COD student records. -Support\n     Military affiliated and Veteran students by connecting them to the Veteran\n     Certifying Official/School Certifying Official (VCO/SCO) on campus. -Summer\n     aid processing, including the manual review of remaining student annual\n     eligibility and manual packaging of Summer aid offers. -Complete\n     Professional Judgement reviews for unique student circumstances including\n     but not limited to Special Circumstances, Actual Expenses, Petitions for\n     Independence, and marital status changes on a case-by-case basis. -Demonstrate\n     and maintain up-to-date knowledge of federal regulations as applicable to\n     federal student aid programs through various training opportunities\n     provided by the U.S. Department of Education, the National Association of\n     Student Financial Aid Administrators, the Idaho Association of Student\n     Financial Aid Administrators, and other professional development opportunities. -May\n     assist with training and professional development of support staff. -Support\n     for federal processes and programs that may include Federal Pell Grant\n     administration, Federal Direct Loan administration (including Schedule of\n     Reductions), Campus Based federal aid administration, alternative loan\n     administration, Prison Education program, Workforce Pell program, etc. -Support\n     for Satisfactory Academic Progress including review of SAP contracts at\n     the conclusion of each semester, review of SAP appeals, and serve as the\n     chair for SAP committees. -Ability\n     to work a regular schedule consistent with the needs of the university is\n     an essential function of this position. This may include some evenings\n     and/or weekends. This may also include some travel (possible overnight). -May\n     be assigned liaison work with other areas on campus or special projects\n     based on operational necessity and individual experience and skills. -All other\n     reasonable duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications -Bachelor’s\n     degree from an accredited institution. -At least two (2) years of financial aid, admissions, academic advising, counseling, or\n     other higher education administration experience. -Knowledge\n     of Federal Title IV regulations. -Knowledge\n     of the Free Application for Federal Student Aid application process. -Strong\n     customer service and interpersonal skills. -Willingness\n     to work some evenings and weekends. -Strong\n     attention to detail. -Presentation/public\n     speaking experience. -Due to the nature of this role, the successful candidate cannot be in\n     default or owe a return of Title IV aid. Preferred Qualifications -Master’s\n     degree from an accredited institution. -Three (3) years of financial aid, admissions, academic advising, counseling, or\n     other higher education administration experience. -Banner ERP\n     experience, specifically the Financial Aid module. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 29, 2026 . Salary will be between $50,000 and $51,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2855 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Student Services Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2851?c=isu": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Occupational Therapy (2937)",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Occupational Therapy (2937) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Clinical Assistant Professor, Occupational Therapy (2937) United States | req2851 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Clinical Assistant Professor, Occupational Therapy (2937) Meridian/Boise NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: January 8, 2027 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description Faculty members are responsible for carrying out matters related to the didactic education program in coordination with the program director. These matters may include: accreditation/certification; program planning and assessment; developing and achieving annual goals/objectives; program marketing and student recruitment; student advising; and fieldwork education. Faculty members also serve as a community contact and representative of the MOT program and faculty. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities This full-time, clinical non-tenure track assistant professor is primarily responsible for the following: •    Teaching in area of expertise and department needs as assigned (60-80%) •    Research portfolio development and study mentoring in support of program priorities (5-15%) •    Service in support of the program, college, university, and profession (10-15%) •    Clinical support in service of program priorities and faculty development (0-20%) •    Travel expectation for onsite teaching at opposite campus (10%) Minimum Qualifications •    Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Occupational Therapy AND Doctoral Degree (Ed.D., pp-OTD, D.Sc., or Ph.D in a related field). Degrees must be awarded by an institution that is accredited by a USDE recognized institutional accrediting agency. •    Three (3) years of documented full-time clinical experience (or equivalent to three years full-time) in the area of pediatric OT practice. •    Current license to practice OT in the state of Idaho or ability to obtain OT licensure in the state of Idaho by applicant’s start date. •    Current NBCOT Certification. •    Current AOTA membership at the time of application (expiration date after anticipated start date). Preferred Qualifications •    At least five (5) years of full-time clinical experience in occupational therapy practice (or the equivalent to five years of full-time experience), with a well-rounded foundation as a generalist OT (anatomy, theory, documentation, activity analysis, and psychosocial and physical function knowledge and skills). •    Advanced certifications related to the practice of occupational therapy or education. •    At least three (3) years of teaching experience, including experience as a fieldwork educator or in higher education within an OT or OTA program. •    Experience with the accreditation process. •    Experience with distance technology to support classroom instruction. •    Evidence of research dissemination and experience mentoring student research projects. •    Experience with mentorship as either a mentor or mentee. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, statement of Teaching Philosophy, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before January 8, 2027 . Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2851 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Faculty Non-Tenure Track Division: Kasiska Division of Health Sciences Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2854?c=isu": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant 2, Meridian Campus (5105)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant 2, Meridian Campus (5105) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Administrative Assistant 2, Meridian Campus (5105) United States | req2854 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/23/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Administrative Assistant 2, Meridian Campus (5105) Meridian/Boise NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To perform complex\nsecretarial, office administration, and public relations assignments; perform\nrelated work. The\nprimary responsibilities of this position include financial processing, invoice\nand payment management, and maintaining accurate financial records in\ncollaboration with campus staff and departments. The position works as part of\na team to support campus operations, including room scheduling, lease\nagreements, and administrative functions. Additional duties include providing\nfront office coverage and assisting the Administrative Services\nManager and Director of Student Services. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities - Process\naccounts payable; paying invoices and creating direct pay requests, reconciling\nPcard, billing for room reservations, and parking. - Billing ‐ Prepare invoices and process payments as needed for facilities\nreservation, photocopier, postage machine, etc. - Room Scheduling ‐ Work with university scheduler to reserve traditional\nclassrooms each semester. Utilize EMS to schedule classrooms, computer labs,\nand conference rooms upon request. - Student Handbook ‐ Work with the Director of Enrollment and Student Services to\nupdate the Student Handbook prior to each semester or as needed. - Travel ‐ Utilize Chrome River system to prepare and submit travel\nauthorizations and reimbursements. - Manage office\nsupply lease agreements, office supplies and Spirit Store inventory. - Process\naccounts receivables. - Assist Administrative Services Manager and Director of Student Services with\ntasks and projects when needed. - Other duties as\nassigned such as annual events; Health Sciences Experience Night and\nCommencement. Minimum Qualifications Good\nknowledge of: - Office support functions\n     including word processing, filing, composing a variety of business\n     documents and reception. - Researching, compiling,\n     and summarizing data for reports. Experience: - Interpreting, applying\n     and explaining complex information such as regulations, policies or\n     services. - Independently solving\n     problems/performing liaison activities in a work setting. - Coordinating activities\n     requiring complex arrangements. Specialty\nItems - Some\npositions at ISU may require one or more of the following: Some knowledge of: - Financial record\n     keeping. - Supervisory practices. Good\nknowledge of: - Legal terminology. - Investigative\n     procedures. Experience: - Public Relations. - Using\n     dictation/transcription equipment & taking minutes. Additional Information ISU minimum for this classification is $19.01/hour, commensurate with education and experience. To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before November 1, 2026. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2854 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2853?c=isu": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant 2, Admissions (1669)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant 2, Admissions (1669) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Administrative Assistant 2, Admissions (1669) United States | req2853 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/23/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Administrative Assistant 2, Admissions (1669) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To perform complex\nsecretarial, office administration, and public relations assignments; perform\nrelated work. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Nature and Scope - These positions perform\nhigh level secretarial duties. - Incumbents have a major role in coordinating\nadministrative activities which requires frequent contact with executives, the\npublic, other agencies and government officials. This requires the incumbent to\nutilize effective public relations and liaison skills. - Incumbents may attend\nmeetings for the administrator to relay and collect information. - Incumbents\nfunction with considerable independence and exercise discretion in applying\npolicies and procedures. - The work requires extensive knowledge of department\nprograms and objectives. - They are responsible for the research, compilation,\nand organization of materials for administrators' use in problem resolution. - These positions are often responsible for ensuring that assignments given to\nother staff by the administrator are completed and timelines are met.\nIncumbents may supervise staff. - These positions independently research,\nanalyze, and compile information to prepare reports, handle complaints, or resolve\nproblems; compose correspondence for supervisor on own initiative or from\ngeneral instructions; format/type a variety of executive, sensitive,\nconfidential, official and/or legal letters and documents. Minimum Qualifications Good\nknowledge of: - Office support functions\n     including word processing, filing, composing a variety of business\n     documents and reception. - Researching, compiling,\n     and summarizing data for reports. Experience: - Interpreting, applying\n     and explaining complex information such as regulations, policies or\n     services. - Independently solving\n     problems/performing liaison activities in a work setting. - Coordinating activities\n     requiring complex arrangements. Specialty\nItems - Some\npositions at ISU may require one or more of the following: Some knowledge of: - Financial record\n     keeping. - Supervisory practices. Good\nknowledge of: - Legal terminology. - Investigative\n     procedures. Experience: - Public Relations. - Using\n     dictation/transcription equipment & taking minutes. Additional Information ISU minimum for this classification is $19.01/hour, commensurate with education and experience. To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before November 8, 2026. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2853 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: Student Services Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2852?c=isu": {
      "title": "Program Information Coordinator, Admissions (1591)",
      "description": "Program Information Coordinator, Admissions (1591) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Program Information Coordinator, Admissions (1591) United States | req2852 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/23/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Program Information Coordinator, Admissions (1591) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To\nmanage, implement, and maintain automated records systems; act as resident\nexpert for a technical agency program; perform liaison duties with internal and\nexternal customers; perform related work. This position serves as a functional expert on the database systems utilized by the Admissions Office and assists the Associate Director of Admissions in ensuring data integrity.  It  advises on system and business processes needed to ensure uniformity and accuracy of data between Recruit CRM and Banner. The position creates edit reports as needed in order to identify and correct data errors and collaborates with other departments and stakeholders as needed to ensure accurate admissions data.  This position requires strong computer and internet research skills, flexibility, and excellent interpersonal communication. This position reports to the Associate Director of Admissions. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities •    Utilizes edit reporting tools such as Advanced Find, Argos Reports and other tools to regularly audit data in Recruit CRM and Banner. •    Creates and maintains dashboards and system views for Admissions staff in Recruit CRM. •    Troubleshoots common errors found in Recruit CRM and Banner for Admissions staff. •    Assists the Associate Director of Admissions with development and implementation of operating policies and procedures related to data systems used by the Office of Admissions. •    Updates and maintains the Undergraduate Admissions Business Process manual and office training materials. •    Works with office staff and Associate Director of Admissions to review business practices on a regular basis to ensure efficiency of processes and uniformity of data. •    Collaborates with the Assistant Director of Admissions Systems and Data Analytics and with Information Technology personnel when needed to ensure data integrity in Recruit CRM and Banner. •    Maintains close contact with other departments and agencies to maintain data integrity and to advise on corrective solutions needed when data integrity problems are found. •    Provides training for office staff for system usage. •    Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Experience: •    That demonstrates good knowledge of manual and automated record management systems. •    Using a personal computer for data management and statistical analyses. •    Interpreting and applying laws, rules, and procedures. •    Performing liaison activities to deal with individuals or resolve conflicts in a work setting. Some\nknowledge of: •    Personal computer trends, capabilities, and terminology. Additional Information I SU minimum for this classification is $21.25/hour, commensurate with education and experience. To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before November 8, 2026. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2852 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: Student Services Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2850?c=isu": {
      "title": "Maintenance Craftsman Senior, Auxiliary Services (2650)",
      "description": "Maintenance Craftsman Senior, Auxiliary Services (2650) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Maintenance Craftsman Senior, Auxiliary Services (2650) United States | req2850 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Maintenance Craftsman Senior, Auxiliary Services (2650) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description To perform skilled trade duties in the operation, maintenance, and repair of buildings and related facilities and systems; perform related work. This position will work within the Auxiliary Services department, which frequently requires staffing events outside the typical workday, including evenings and weekends. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Examples of Duties 1. Facility maintenance. Electrical. -Maintains and repairs panels, circuits, wiring, and related systems. -Replaces switches, receptacles, ballast's, fuse boxes, heat systems, motors, fans and lights. -Repairs electric motors and extension cords. -Installs communication cable and telephone lines. -Assists journeyman electricians in new installations. Plumbing. -Maintains and repairs plumbing fixtures, lavatories, faucets, sinks, tubs, water heaters and water service and drain lines. -Installs domestic, irrigation, and sprinkler systems. -Cleans/unclogs pipes, tanks, floor drains and sewers. -Cuts and threads or sweats pipe. -Repairs steam traps and pipes on heat systems. -Conducts preventive maintenance of plumbing and steam systems. -Assists journeyman plumbers in the installation and remodeling of plumbing systems. Carpentry. -Installs ceramic floor and wall tile, linoleum, plastic laminate and similar products. -Repairs built-up, shake, shingle, and other roofs. -Patches holes in walls using sheetrock, plywood, tile, and plaster. -Reglazes windows. -Builds walls, partitions, benches, decks, and tables. -Sketches from oral instructions and works from drawings to design and build specialty items. -Builds and sets forms and pours and finishes concrete. -Builds fences and gates. HVAC. -Maintains and repairs heating, ventilating, and air conditioning equipment such as air compressors, dryers, strainers, pneumatic and electronic controls and piping systems. -Insures water and steam coils, motors, belts, pulleys, condenser pans, duct work, dampers, and related systems are working properly. -Repairs fire alarm and pumping systems. 2. Miscellaneous. -Conducts preventive maintenance on building devices and systems. -Operates equipment used in building maintenance and repair. -Performs machinist work involving design and fabrication of specialized parts and equipment. -Welds and repairs and fabricates brackets, fixtures, and similar items. -Rebuilds motors and performs mechanical and preventive maintenance work on equipment. -Lays brick, stone, and block. -Removes debris from area. -Repairs appliances. -Responds to emergency call-backs. -Functions as leadworker over other maintenance staff and assists with general related trade duties. Minimum Qualifications Good knowledge of: - Carpentry, plumbing, electrical and general building maintenance. Some knowledge of: - HVAC and mechanical systems maintenance. - Building codes. Experience: -Performing skilled carpentry, plumbing, electrical, and building maintenance repair. -Using and maintaining tools and equipment normally associated with carpentry, mechanics, plumbing, and electrical work. -Reading blueprints and schematics. Specialty Items: - These positions at ISU require a valid standard driver's license. - These positions on the Pocatello campus require the ability to demonstrate successful completion of both a physical exam, including cardiopulmonary function testing and chest x-ray, and a respirator fit test. Supplemental Information - Incumbents work in all weather conditions and move in and around confined spaces. These positions are maintenance oriented. - When working under the supervision of a licensed journeyman in a respective trade area incumbents can be an apprentice in that specialty. - These positions involve lifting and carrying items weighing approximately 90 pounds, bending, stooping, shoveling, and climbing ladders. - Incumbents respond to emergency call-backs. Additional Information I SU minimum for this classification is $17.25/hour, commensurate with education and experience. To be considered for this opportunity, apply on or before November 5, 2026. Benefits include comprehensive health, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance program (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and generous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are conditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation, provided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2850 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Classified Staff Division: OPERATIONS Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2847?c=isu": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Political Science (3450)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Political Science (3450) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate Professor, Political Science (3450) United States | req2847 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Assistant/Associate Professor, Political Science (3450) Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Review of applications will begin January 4, 2027 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description Idaho State University (ISU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in the Department of Political Science specializing in public administration to begin in August 2027. The department seeks a candidate who can contribute primarily to its growing MPA program, including serving as MPA Director, as well as opportunities to teach courses in the undergraduate and other graduate  (MA, DA) political science programs. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities The position carries a 3-3 teaching load. Faculty will also have service and research obligations, which comprise 40 percent of the workload. Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or equivalent) in Political\nScience, Public Administration, Public Policy, or a closely related field by\nthe start of the Fall 2027 semester. Candidates who are ABD will be considered,\nprovided all degree requirements are successfully completed prior to the start\nof classes in Fall 2027. Preferred Qualifications Candidates who can teach some combination of the following courses are preferred: Introduction to Public Administration, Human Resource Management, Public Policy Analysis, Public Administration Ethics, Nonprofit Management, Grantwriting, Community and Regional Planning, Program Assessment and Evaluation, and MPA Capstone. Candidates with an MPA degree or who have completed comprehensive exams in public administration are preferred. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before January 4, 2027 . Salary will be between $66,000 and $75,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2847 Type: Working 9 months per year Position: Faculty Tenure Track Division: Office Of Academic Affairs Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2849?c=isu": {
      "title": "IT Device Support Supervisor, ITS",
      "description": "IT Device Support Supervisor, ITS | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) IT Device Support Supervisor, ITS United States | req2849 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . IT Device Support Supervisor, ITS Pocatello - Main NOT eligible for remote work, on-campus position Priority Date: November 2, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description This is a promotional opportunity for current employees of Idaho State University only. The IT Device Support Supervisor provides operational leadership and strategic direction as the university’s primary point of contact for device management and support. This role manages a versatile team of full-time staff and student technicians to deliver consistent service quality to faculty, staff, and students, efficient workflows, and achievement of key performance goals through active supervision, coaching and performance monitoring. This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities 1. Team Leadership & Student Development (40%) ● Recruit, onboard, and mentor a team of 10-20 student employees and 2-4 full-time staff. ● Foster a \"teaching hospital\" environment where student workers gain professional IT skills while providing tier-2 device support. ● Manage complex shift scheduling to ensure consistent device support availability. 2. Operational Management (30%) ● Supervises the day-to-day operations of the Device Services staff to maximize team effectiveness and meet business needs. ● Oversee the resolution of complex hardware, software, mobile, and peripheral device issues escalated from Tier 1. ● Manage and refine automated self-service workflows to ensure timely device setup and support. 3. Technical Oversight & Documentation (20%) ● Act as the final escalation point for \"high-touch\" users, including University Executives and Faculty during critical academic periods. ● Resolves escalated problems referred by subordinate staff and notifies the director of issues that require review. ● Maintain a robust Knowledge Base (KB) for both internal staff training and public-facing \"How-To\" and “FAQ” guides relating to Tier 2 support. ● Partner with Infrastructure and Security teams to remediate campus-wide outages or cybersecurity threats. ● Collaborate with other ITS Supervisors on emerging trends, workarounds, and fixes emerging issues. 4. Project Management (10%) ● Lead readiness projects for new semesters. ● Lead device rollouts as dictated by device refresh cycles. Other Duties: ● Performs other job-related duties as assigned. ● May provide after-hours coverage or on-call supervision as assigned. Minimum Qualifications ● Current ISU Employee. ● Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (in lieu of a Bachelor’s Degree, a minimum of six years combined education, training, and experience may be considered). ● Three (3+) years of experience in an IT device support environment, with at least 1 year in a supervisory or lead capacity. ● Deep knowledge of operating systems (Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, Android), mobile device management (MDM), and hardware diagnostics. ● Experience with Enterprise systems (O365, Google Workspace, Box). ● Experience with various hardware (Dell, Apple, printers). Preferred Qualifications ● Previous experience working in a Higher Education setting. ● Proven experience managing or mentoring student/intern teams. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 2, 2026 . Salary will be between $60,000 - $65,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2849 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: Information Technology Services Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://isu.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/5/home/requisition/2848?c=isu": {
      "title": "Senior Prospect Research Analyst, University Advancement (2880)",
      "description": "Senior Prospect Research Analyst, University Advancement (2880) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Senior Prospect Research Analyst, University Advancement (2880) United States | req2848 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/16/2026 Back to Search Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Senior Prospect Research Analyst, University Advancement (2880) Pocatello - Main May\nbe eligible for remote work from Idaho, Wyoming or Utah as approved by hiring manager. Priority Date: November 1, 2026 Institution Information Idaho State University, established in 1901, is a\nCarnegie-classified doctoral research and teaching institution, with a culture\nbuilt on trust, compassion, stability, and hope. ISU serves over 12,000\nstudents in Pocatello, Meridian, Twin Falls, and Idaho Falls. Students and\nfaculty at ISU are leading the way in cutting-edge research and innovative\nsolutions. We are proud to offer exceptional academics nestled in the grand,\nnatural beauty of the West. We invite you to apply to be a part of our\nUniversity community! Job Description The ISU Foundation serves as the fundraising and advancement partner of Idaho State University, securing and stewarding private support that strengthens the University’s mission and impact. The Foundation is committed to fostering a culture defined by empowerment, appreciation, engagement, and accountability, cornerstones that guide how we work, collaborate, and celebrate success. Our team values trust and shared purpose as we build a strategic and sustainable advancement organization. Together, we cultivate relationships that connect donors, alumni, and partners to the transformative work taking place across the University. Idaho State University and the ISU Foundation are actively preparing to launch a historic and ambitious comprehensive fundraising campaign. The Senior Prospect Research Analyst is a strategic partner to fundraising leadership and Directors of Development. The role leads the quarterly portfolio review program, advances moves-management discipline across principal and major gift portfolios, and delivers high‑quality research, analysis, and briefings that accelerate philanthropic outcomes. The ideal candidate blends traditional prospect research with modern data analytics, translating internal and external signals into clear recommendations that drive action. Reports to: Director, Foundation Data and Research Supervises: Prospect Research Analyst This position is not eligible for new visa sponsorship at this time. Candidates who already hold valid U.S. work authorization may be considered. Key Responsibilities Portfolio Management and Moves Strategy ● Co-lead the quarterly portfolio review process: prepare coverage and activity dashboards; facilitate review meetings; document adds/drops, next steps, and accountability follow-ups. ● Maintain the Portfolio Guide (stage definitions, movement expectations, contact/visit cadence, portfolio size/coverage targets) in partnership with the Director. ● Monitor pipeline health (stage aging, coverage ratios, proposal velocity) and recommend portfolio right-sizing and reallocations. ● Support moves management discipline: surface next best actions, create call sheets/prep briefs, and coordinate with gift officers and leadership on movement plans. Prospect Research and Intelligence ● Continuously strengthen ISU’s prospect pipeline by combining internal Foundation’s data with vetted public sources to surface affinity, interests, and philanthropic capacity. ● Apply structured research methods to analyze financial and biographical indicators; produce decision-ready profiles and strategy notes; and recommend the next, highest-impact actions for each prospect. ● Scan news and market signals and translate relevant developments into prospect strategies aligned to ISU priorities (academics, athletics, scholarships, capital projects). ● Produce concise, executive-ready briefs for priority visits and solicitations Data Stewardship, Reporting and Audits. ● Audit principal and major gift pools, portfolios, and proposals to ensure accuracy, deduplication, and stage integrity. ● Partner with Data Analyst to produce routine portfolio and pipeline reporting, including activity, coverage, and outcomes by unit and fundraiser. ● Ensure compliance with privacy, CASE standards, and institutional policies; document sources and methodologies for repeatability and audit readiness. Collaboration, Training and Standards ● Serve as a strategic partner to the development team; provide ongoing research, qualification lists, and cultivation/solicitation strategies. ● Review and refine research deliverables for clarity, sourcing, and tone; uphold team style and citation standards. ● Coach a Prospect Research Analyst and student staff; deliver practical training on research methods, brief writing, and moves-management basics. ● Contribute to a learning culture by sharing best practices with Advancement and Foundation colleagues and building peer networks across institutions. Continuous Improvement ● Pursue targeted professional learning (e.g., Apra/CASE sessions and peer exchanges) and incorporate takeaways into team playbooks. ● Develop and refine templates, playbooks, and SOPs that scale prospecting, qualification, and portfolio hygiene across the division. Minimum Qualifications ● Bachelor’s\ndegree in Business, Communications, Social Sciences, Library/Information\nScience, Data Analytics, or a related discipline, plus a minimum of (3) years\nof progressively responsible relevant professional experience. In lieu of a Bachelor’s\ndegree, at least nine (9) years of direct, relevant professional experience may\nbe considered (where six (6) years of experience substitutes for the degree\nrequirement, in addition to three (3) years of required role experience). ● At least one (1) year mentoring and supervisory experience. ● Demonstrated ability to synthesize qualitative and quantitative data into clear, actionable insights and recommendations. ● Strong writing and editing skills; experience producing executive-ready briefs and strategy documents. ● Experience with CRM/advancement systems (e.g., Raiser’s Edge NXT or similar), wealth screening and research tools, and advanced Excel/Google Sheets. Preferred Qualifications ● Experience supporting principal gifts and complex, multi-stakeholder strategies. ● Knowledge of CASE Global Reporting Standards and advancement best practices (prospect stages, pipeline metrics, portfolio coverage). ● Experience supporting comprehensive fundraising campaigns. ● Experience working in philanthropy in a higher education and/or non-profit setting. ●The ideal candidate is an outcomes‑focused research partner who turns data and context into clear next steps for fundraisers. Grounded in confidentiality and professional standards, they ask smart questions, surface risks and opportunities, and improve processes with reusable templates and SOPs. Collaborative, curious, and reliable, they help move prospects through the pipeline and advance ISU’s fundraising priorities. If you thrive in a collaborative environment and are inspired by the opportunity to help shape the future of Idaho State University, we encourage you to apply and join our Advancement and Foundation team. Additional Information Y ou must submit your CV/resume, cover letter, and list of\nthree (3) professional references, including current contact information. This\nposition will remain open until it is filled; however, priority consideration\nwill be given to applications received on or before November 1, 2026 . Salary will be between $65,000 and $75,000 per year,\ncommensurate with education and experience. Benefits include comprehensive\nhealth, dental, and vision; life insurance; disability plan; employee assistance\nprogram (EAP); excellent retirement options and company contribution; and\ngenerous paid time off/sick leave accrual. All offers of employment are\nconditional pending the successful completion of a background investigation,\nprovided by HireRight. Note: Thank you for your interest in positions at Idaho State University. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by logging into your profile and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions, please review our frequently asked questions . Posting Number: req2848 Type: Working 12 months per year Position: Non-classified Staff Division: University Advancement Idaho State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, including Veterans and individuals with disabilities. The State of Idaho is committed to access and reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities, auxiliary aids and services are available upon request. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 334-2263 (TTY/TTD: 711), or email ada.coordinator@dhr.idaho.gov. Preference may be given to veterans who qualify under state and federal laws and regulations. _____________________________________________________________________________________________ Apply Now Share Save Job"
    }
  },
  "rows": {
